in the integral domain $F_{147457}[t]$. Thus either the specialized factor $F$ or the specialized complementary factor $G$ is zero, and in either case
$$(A/F)(L(t),P_L(t))=0.$$
The quotient is a nonzero kernel element, and the preceding application of KTZ Lemma 2.5 shows that it remains $Z$-dependent. Its weighted degree is smaller than that of $A$, contradicting minimality. Hence $A$ is squarefree.38:T83d,Write $A=CB$, where $C\in F_{147457}[X,Y]$ is the coefficient content of $A$ in $Z$ and $B$ is primitive. Put
$$h=\deg C,
\qquad W=\operatorname{wdeg}_{(1,1,87)}B,
