=\frac{67333805766276738068309588974841569}{153293031444312855941000000000000000000000000000000}>0.$$
Consequently, complete deletion would imply $|E|/N<\epsilon$, contrary to the hypothesis. The core is nonempty. The peeling thresholds give minimum point degree $D+1=17643$ and minimum line degree $s=5495$. Exceptional lines and derivative-zero incidences were removed, so every retained line has a formal $B$-identity and every retained edge satisfies $B_Z(x,f(x))\ne0$.3a:T6d8,Fix a component, and let $a$ and $b$ be its point and line densities. Let $\eta$ be its retained-edge count normalized by
