Some choice of $S$ attains at least this expectation.43:T4e1,The bidegree bound gives $\deg Q\le174$. Suppose that the top total degree is $T$ with $88\le T\le174$, and let $H_T$ be the nonzero homogeneous part of degree $T$. A nonzero binary homogeneous form of degree $T$ vanishes on at most $T$ projective directions. Thus $H_T$ is nonzero on at least $147458-T$ directions.

