This contradicts the acceptance hypothesis. Therefore the top total degree is at most $87$.44:T71a,Choose coordinates in which the anchor lines have equations $X=a_i$ and the crossing lines have equations $Y=b$. Interpolate the $88$ anchor labels in the $X$ variable. Since the $a_i$ are distinct, all Lagrange denominators are nonzero, and this produces a unique polynomial $Q$ of bidegree at most $(87,87)$ whose restriction to every anchor line is its supplied label.

On a crossing line $Y=b$, both $Q(X,b)$ and the supplied crossing label have degree at most $87$ in $X$. They agree at the $88$ intersections with the anchor lines, so they coincide identically.

