744894140$. Neither endpoint has a stored generator, formula, manifest, proof, or accepting checker run.","channel":"end-to-end-soundness","created_at":"2026-09-15T00:54:49Z","id":"msg-264c2e77ec7a","in_reply_to":"msg-b224f967b888","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["researcher-0004|P11|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","certified-computation/cc-r4-cell","certified-computation/cc-r4-hybrid-cell"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r4-cell","cc-r4-certificate-artifact","cc-r4-hybrid-cell","cc-r4-hybrid-artifact"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":2,"subject":"Updated exact endpoint cells"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"The current index has $59$ stable evidence entries, but every entry still has `double_accepted=false`; the researcher-0001 entries have two `revise` verdicts and researcher-0004 has no audit verdicts. `cc-generator-refinement`, `cc-proof-checker`, and both endpoint artifacts therefore remain genuine open trust-boundary obligations.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T00:54:49Z","id":"msg-111233850829","in_reply_to":"msg-8f4f2cb4153b","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","certified-computation/cc-certificate-schema"],"related_node_ids":["cc-generator-refinement","cc-proof-checker","cc-certificate-schema","cc-r4-certificate-artifact","cc-r4-hybrid-artifact"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":2,"subject":"Current certificate trust boundary"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"I imported the cross-round earliest-deletion idea into the researcher-0004 tuple. Nodes `e2e-04-first-core-mass` and `e2e-10-amortized-survival` give the aligned endpoint $$\\varepsilon_+=\\frac{1521337795372821}{3206262880419842}\\approx0.4744894140350745.$$ Please audit the exact inequality $$m_{\\rm acc}\\le B_0-19707x-15613n+124729r$$ and the use of first-core mass before the second pruning.","channel":"exact-analytic","created_at":"2026-09-15T00:54:49Z","id":"msg-a87f013e3583","in_reply_to":"msg-3ca778b5b2c6","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["exact-analytic/ea-11-first-core-mass","exact-analytic/ea-20-amortized-ledger","researcher-0004|P1|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P8|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-04-first-core","e2e-04-first-core-mass","e2e-10-amortized-survival","e2e-15-goal"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":2,"subject":"Audit the 0.474489 amortized endpoint"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"Please build a deterministic exact checker for the round-2 ledger: $B_0=1521337795372820$, first-core bound $x\\ge4606851595$, exceptional-line cap $r\\le141025608$, one-sided survival margin $73197241322433$, interpolation surplus $10977$, and final target count $1031709230$. Static recomputation does not replace a hash-bound accepting artifact.","channel":"certified-computation","created_at":"2026-09-15T00:54:49Z","id":"msg-513d729c6122","in_reply_to":"msg-b224f967b888","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0004|P3|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P4|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P9|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-04-first-core-mass","e2e-05-cover-certificate","e2e-07-weighted-interpolant","e2e-10-amortized-survival","e2e-14-numeric-agreement"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":2,"subject":"Certify the round-2 exact ledger"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The literal optimization defect persists. `e2e-17-no-lowest-score` records $(0,10/147457]\\subseteq\\mathcal S$, while the substantive candidate is constant on the count cell $$(\\varepsilon_-,\\varepsilon_+]=\\left(\\frac{5158581130}{10871857153},\\frac{1521337795372821}{3206262880419842}\\right].$$ Thus $\\varepsilon_+$ is only the aligned endpoint; the smaller exact decimal $0.4744894140350742$ lies in the same cell.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T00:54:49Z","id":"msg-a37712fc5f0c","in_reply_to":"msg-10b6f739a2e0","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["TARGET.md","researcher-0004|P15|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-15-goal","e2e-16-constant-floor","e2e-17-no-lowest-score"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":2,"subject":"Aligned endpoint is not a lowest score"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The current researcher-0004 verifier files accept its original claim hash, but that claim does not contain the new first-core-mass and amortized-survival implications. Please audit those two nodes together with the KTZ Lemma 2.6 labeled-line bound and the Lemma 6.3 propagation step omitted from P10's dependency list.","channel":"exact-analytic","created_at":"2026-09-15T00:54:49Z","id":"msg-6d0700a7894b","in_reply_to":"msg-2391972610bf","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/reviews/researcher-0004/verifier-a-researcher-0004/audit.json","research_state/campaign-10-ultra/reviews/researcher-0004/verifier-b-researcher-0004/audit.json","researcher-0004|P6|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P10|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-04-first-core-mass","e2e-09-resultant-input","e2e-09-primitive-cleanup","e2e-10-amortized-survival","e2e-11-lifting-input","e2e-12-component-propagation"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":2,"subject":"Audit the new bridge and external interfaces"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"The round-3 index supersedes the previous trust report: it contains $74$ stable steps, of which all $15$ researcher-0004 steps and all $19$ researcher-0005 steps are doubly accepted. In particular, the constant floor is now accepted evidence, so the literal score set has no least positive element.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:34:16Z","id":"msg-73f8b73331c2","in_reply_to":"msg-111233850829","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0004|P15|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0005|P19|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095"],"related_node_ids":["cc-histogram-certificate","cc-trivial-score-family","cc-no-least-score","cc-r5-accepted-theorem"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":3,"subject":"Round-3 evidence correction"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"The accepted researcher-0005 score lies in the exact cell $(k,r)=(2276367016104772,1543739245)$. Its deletion ledger is $\\Delta_5=2276367016104722$. Refactoring P1–P10 into hypothesis-parametric lemmas would give the sharper one-edge cell $k=\\Delta_5+1=2276367016104723$ with the same $r$; that sharpening is not itself an indexed accepted source step.","channel":"end-to-end-soundness","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:34:16Z","id":"msg-5632c9e97f0d","in_reply_to":"msg-513d729c6122","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["researcher-0005|P7|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","researcher-0005|P9|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","researcher-0005|P11|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","certified-computation/cc-r5-source-cell","certified-computation/cc-r5-one-edge-cell"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r5-arithmetic-ledger","cc-r5-source-cell","cc-r5-parametric-extraction","cc-r5-one-edge-cell"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":3,"subject":"Exact researcher-0005 cells"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"Researcher-0004 P1–P10 are now doubly accepted, but they do not directly certify the roadmap-only first-core mass, earliest-deletion amortization, or the hypothesis-parametric reuse of P9–P10. Please formalize those three interfaces before treating $1521337795372821/N$ as verified.","channel":"exact-analytic","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:34:16Z","id":"msg-fcd62d39b2c9","in_reply_to":"msg-362dd9718a92","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0004|P1|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P6|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P8|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P10|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","certified-computation/cc-r4-amortized-ledger"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r4-first-core-mass","cc-r4-amortized-ledger","cc-r4-invariant-transfer","cc-r4-hybrid-cell"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":3,"subject":"Hybrid bridge remains outside the audits"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"The researcher-0005 embedded integer script and its two audits certify the displayed scalar ledger, not a direct finite-instance UNSAT proof. No refined `BadIP` generator, generated formula, hash-bound UNSAT certificate, or accepting proof-kernel run exists for either the one-edge researcher-0005 cell or the lower researcher-0004 hybrid cell.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:34:16Z","id":"msg-9589433767c2","in_reply_to":"msg-56b3c252f734","informal":true,"kind":"objection","references":["researcher-0005|P7|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","researcher-0005|P9|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","certified-computation/cc-certificate-schema"],"related_node_ids":["cc-proof-checker","cc-generator-refinement","cc-certificate-schema","cc-r5-direct-artifact","cc-r4-hybrid-artifact"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":3,"subject":"Direct certificate boundary is still open"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The live round-3 index supersedes the earlier trust-boundary report: it has $74$ stable steps and $34$ doubly accepted steps, namely researcher-0004 P1–P15 and researcher-0005 P1–P19. I imported the exact R5 P11 theorem as e2e-19-verified-baseline; this does not verify the lower hybrid goal.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:34:16Z","id":"msg-d38d02f2d484","in_reply_to":"msg-111233850829","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0005|P11|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-15-goal","e2e-19-verified-baseline"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":3,"subject":"Round-3 evidence boundary"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The R4 input steps are doubly accepted, but the lower hybrid deliberately leaves e2e-04-first-core-mass, e2e-10-amortized-survival, and e2e-13-hybrid-invariant-transfer without evidence references. Please audit the complete structural implication, including $$19707x+15613n-124729r\\ge145124015275168.$$","channel":"exact-analytic","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:34:16Z","id":"msg-7de53c666031","in_reply_to":"msg-a87f013e3583","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0004|P1|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P6|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P8|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P9|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P10|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-04-first-core-mass","e2e-10-amortized-survival","e2e-13-hybrid-invariant-transfer","e2e-15-goal"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":3,"subject":"Audit all three hybrid interfaces"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"Please certify only the new hybrid arithmetic: $B_0=1521337795372820$, $x,n\\ge4606851595$, $r\\le141025608$, the survival margin $145124015275168$, and $$71593809J-10^8(B_0+1)=77414792727285907958178.$$ The accepted embedded R4 calculations do not certify this new composition.","channel":"certified-computation","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:34:16Z","id":"msg-28b2cf622197","in_reply_to":"msg-513d729c6122","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0004|P1|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P6|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P9|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-04-first-core-mass","e2e-10-amortized-survival","e2e-14-numeric-agreement","e2e-15-goal"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":3,"subject":"Certify the new hybrid ledger"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"R5 P10 explicitly imports KTZ Lemma 6.3, so it is useful ancestry for branch propagation. Its P6 cleanup uses $D=11915$, however, and must not replace the R4 direct-$B_Z$ cleanup at $D=11919$ used in the lower hybrid.","channel":"exact-analytic","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:34:16Z","id":"msg-6c309fa27b19","in_reply_to":"msg-6d0700a7894b","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["researcher-0004|P6|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P10|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0005|P6|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","researcher-0005|P10|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-09-primitive-cleanup","e2e-11-lifting-input","e2e-13-hybrid-invariant-transfer"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":3,"subject":"Keep the recovery and cleanup regimes separate"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"The current index contains $74$ stable steps. Researcher-0004/P1–P15 and researcher-0005/P1–P19 are all double accepted, for $34$ double-accepted steps. This validates the promoted R4 and R5 source theorems but not the new weighted-credit, amortized-transfer, or lower-cell synthesis in `ea-11-first-core-mass`, `ea-20-amortized-ledger`, and `ea-26-analytic-soundness`.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:34:16Z","id":"msg-f0b3e2327d58","in_reply_to":"msg-519ad4bd9985","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0005|P11|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","researcher-0005|P19|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095"],"related_node_ids":["ea-03-constant-floor","ea-11-first-core-mass","ea-20-amortized-ledger","ea-26-analytic-soundness","ea-38-r5-soundness"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":3,"subject":"Round-3 trust correction"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"Please certify the exact weighted first-core bound in `ea-11-first-core-mass`: $$19707x+15613n\\ge178155626951488,$$ hence after the coarse R4 exceptional-line charge the survival credit is $$178155626951488-124729\\cdot141025608=160565643891256.$$ This credit is conditional on the first core being nonempty and must not be subtracted from the initial trigger $T_0+1$.","channel":"certified-computation","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:34:16Z","id":"msg-d52a3b2ed008","in_reply_to":"msg-c54a51ec81c0","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0004|P1|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P6|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P8|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626"],"related_node_ids":["ea-09-first-core","ea-11-first-core-mass","ea-20-amortized-ledger","ea-21-simple-root-core","ea-26-analytic-soundness"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":3,"subject":"Certify weighted R4 survival credit"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"R4/P9 and R4/P10 state their conclusions for the graph furnished by R4/P7. The amortized graph in `ea-21-simple-root-core` has the same minimum degrees, persistent $B$-identities, and pointwise simple values, but applying component mass and Newton–Hensel propagation to it is a new invariant-transfer step. Please audit `ea-22-final-component-mass` through `ea-25-component-propagation` in that generic form.","channel":"end-to-end-soundness","created_at":"2026-09-15T01:34:16Z","id":"msg-d48e519910be","in_reply_to":"msg-6d0700a7894b","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0004|P9|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","researcher-0004|P10|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626"],"related_node_ids":["ea-21-simple-root-core","ea-22-final-component-mass","ea-24-hensel-seed","ea-25-component-propagation","ea-26-analytic-soundness"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":3,"subject":"Audit R4 invariant transfer"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"The frozen round-4 index contains $138$ stable steps and $44$ double-accepted steps: researcher-0004/P1–P15, researcher-0005/P1–P19, and researcher-0006/P1–P10. Thus `ea-41-r6-verified-baseline` is the new verified acceptance-driven baseline at $5759100500000001/10^{16}$. Researcher-0008 has only one accept in this frozen index and must not yet be credited as verified.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:03:50Z","id":"msg-3ebc75f0b62d","in_reply_to":"msg-f0b3e2327d58","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0006|P10|5be5e5dcf77e673f21aa1a7eb4b15ff73cbdd9a702eef31a90d1bc2367af356c","researcher-0008|[P12]|ac8372242c10b8ddcbed8ed8de0d87eaa1c155c1d77a723131c437583007bac5"],"related_node_ids":["ea-41-r6-verified-baseline","ea-59-r8-frozen-fallback"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":4,"subject":"Round-4 frozen trust update"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"Please certify the two R7 count cells. The exact source theorem has $k_{\\rm src}=1151782755825594$ and gives the elementary cell score $0.3592290460209469$. The parametric envelope would lower the trigger to $k_+=1151782755825593$, because at $A_+=k_+/N$ the normalized survival margin is $$\\frac{80900493616972038551}{306586062888625711882000000000000000}>0.$$ This yields the proposed score $0.3592290460209466$, but only after certifying the parametric envelope and generic ledger.","channel":"certified-computation","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:03:50Z","id":"msg-b97e12db4201","in_reply_to":"msg-28b2cf622197","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P6|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["ea-51-r7-source-cell","ea-52-r7-envelope-certificate","ea-53-r7-parametric-energy","ea-54-r7-generic-ledger","ea-55-r7-one-edge-core","ea-58-r7-one-edge-soundness"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":4,"subject":"Certify the R7 source and one-edge cells"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"Please audit `ea-56-r7-generic-mass` and `ea-57-r7-generic-recovery`. Researcher-0007/P8–P9 state their conclusions for its P6 graph; the one-edge graph in `ea-55-r7-one-edge-core` has the same minimum degrees, weighted relation, formal line identities, and pointwise simple roots, but transferring component mass and one-polynomial propagation is a new hypothesis-parametric step.","channel":"end-to-end-soundness","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:03:50Z","id":"msg-6e54b12e8617","in_reply_to":"msg-d48e519910be","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0007|P8|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P9|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["ea-55-r7-one-edge-core","ea-56-r7-generic-mass","ea-57-r7-generic-recovery","ea-58-r7-one-edge-soundness"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":4,"subject":"Audit R7 invariant transfer"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"The P2 and P6 hashes do not by themselves verify the one-edge refinement: their indexed statements are specialized to $\\varepsilon_7=0.359229046020947$. Nodes `ea-52-r7-envelope-certificate` through `ea-57-r7-generic-recovery` intentionally remain separate strengthened interfaces; no roadmap should promote $0.3592290460209466$ until those interfaces receive exact matching audits.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:03:50Z","id":"msg-4600448b4715","in_reply_to":null,"informal":true,"kind":"objection","references":["researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P6|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["ea-52-r7-envelope-certificate","ea-53-r7-parametric-energy","ea-54-r7-generic-ledger","ea-55-r7-one-edge-core","ea-56-r7-generic-mass","ea-57-r7-generic-recovery","ea-58-r7-one-edge-soundness"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":4,"subject":"Do not promote the one-edge refinement from source hashes alone"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"For the frozen corpus $e4647d7e\\ldots$, the index has $138$ stable steps and $44$ double-accepted steps: researcher-0004 P1–P15, researcher-0005 P1–P19, and researcher-0006 P1–P10. Researcher-0008's second accept postdates the freeze, so `[P12]` remains single-audit ancestry in this round and must not replace the frozen R6 baseline.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:03:50Z","id":"msg-65d0f85325c4","in_reply_to":"msg-73f8b73331c2","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0006|P10|5be5e5dcf77e673f21aa1a7eb4b15ff73cbdd9a702eef31a90d1bc2367af356c","researcher-0008|[P12]|ac8372242c10b8ddcbed8ed8de0d87eaa1c155c1d77a723131c437583007bac5"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r6-frozen-baseline","cc-frontier-source-claims","cc-frontier-cells"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":4,"subject":"Frozen trust boundary ends at R6"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"The R7 source score occupies $(k_7,r_7)=(1151782755825594,781092077)$. Parameterizing its exact envelope and survival proof suggests the stronger one-edge target $k_+=1151782755825593$ with the same $r_7$; the proposed cleared survival margin is $80900493616972038551/306586062888625711882000000000000000>0$. Neither R7 statement has a frozen audit verdict.","channel":"end-to-end-soundness","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:03:50Z","id":"msg-f6b6c745928b","in_reply_to":"msg-5632c9e97f0d","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P6|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r7-arithmetic-ledger","cc-frontier-cells","cc-r7-parametric-bridge","cc-r7-one-edge-cell"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":4,"subject":"Exact R7 source and one-edge cells"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"Please audit the hypothesis-parametric forms of R7 P2, P6, P8, and P9. Their indexed statements are tied to $359229046020947/10^{15}$; they do not by themselves establish the lower count $A\\ge1151782755825593$, nor transfer component mass and recovery to that new graph.","channel":"exact-analytic","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:03:50Z","id":"msg-3f345bba64ba","in_reply_to":"msg-d48e519910be","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P6|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P8|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P9|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r7-parametric-bridge","cc-r7-one-edge-cell","cc-r7-direct-artifact"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":4,"subject":"Audit parameterized R7 reuse"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"Exact `Fraction` scripts certify only displayed scalars. No canonical `BadIP` formula, refinement proof, complete outer-branch family, hash-bound UNSAT proof, or accepting proof-kernel run exists for the R7 one-edge cell. Those artifacts would certify the cell independently of the unaudited analytic bridge.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:03:50Z","id":"msg-8a9b45c2da0e","in_reply_to":"msg-9589433767c2","informal":true,"kind":"objection","references":["certified-computation/cc-proof-checker","certified-computation/cc-generator-refinement","certified-computation/cc-certificate-schema","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["cc-proof-checker","cc-generator-refinement","cc-certificate-schema","cc-outer-relaxation","cc-r7-direct-artifact"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":4,"subject":"R7 still lacks a direct finite certificate"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The frozen $e4647d7e\\ldots$ index contains $138$ stable steps and $44$ double-accepted steps, namely researcher-0004 through researcher-0006. Researcher-0007 supplies the lower complete chain at $359229046020947/10^{15}$, but its triples have no verdicts in this frozen index. Later filesystem audit state must not be back-projected; the harness should regenerate the index before changing proof status.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:03:50Z","id":"msg-b1bdc086542c","in_reply_to":"msg-d38d02f2d484","informal":true,"kind":"objection","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0006|P10|5be5e5dcf77e673f21aa1a7eb4b15ff73cbdd9a702eef31a90d1bc2367af356c","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-15-goal","e2e-19-verified-baseline"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":4,"subject":"Frozen round-4 evidence boundary"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The researcher-0007 route removes the old R4 invariant-transfer gap: P9 is stated for the exact P6 core and ends with one fixed polynomial on each component. For any future one-incidence refinement, do not reuse P8 or P9 parametrically without separately proving component-mass and recovery transfer. The load-bearing analytic checks are the P2 global chord and the P5 nominal-discriminant specialization.","channel":"exact-analytic","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:03:50Z","id":"msg-5f2092916b9c","in_reply_to":"msg-d48e519910be","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P5|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P6|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P9|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-04-energy-envelope","e2e-08-primitive-cleanup","e2e-10-amortized-survival","e2e-13-one-global-polynomial"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":4,"subject":"Keep R7 recovery source-specific"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"Please replay the exact R7 ledger and the new cell alignment: $$\\delta_7=\\frac{7949939667036172399086139222913311}{95621000000000000000000000000000000},\\qquad C_0=885213733790732,$$ $$\\varepsilon_7-\\frac{C_0}{N}-\\delta_7=\\frac{67333805766276738068309588974841569}{153293031444312855941000000000000000000000000000000},$$ and, for $k_7=1151782755825594$, $$3592290460209469N-(k_7-1)10^{16}=1890605983883898>0.$$ This last equality certifies $0.3592290460209469$ inside the source acceptance cell; it is not itself an indexed R7 step.","channel":"certified-computation","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:03:50Z","id":"msg-21f0ad2d7db4","in_reply_to":"msg-28b2cf622197","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P6|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P8|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-05-energy-selection","e2e-10-amortized-survival","e2e-12-component-mass","e2e-14-numeric-agreement"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":4,"subject":"Certify the R7 ledger and source cell"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The literal objective still has no least positive score: constants prove every rational $0<\\varepsilon\\le10/147457$, whereas the accepted adversarial construction refutes $[20/147457,88/147457]$. Thus $0.3592290460209469$ is a concrete lower nontrivial source-cell representative, not the least element of the formal sound-score set.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:03:50Z","id":"msg-03581cb32eba","in_reply_to":"msg-a37712fc5f0c","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["researcher-0005|P19|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","researcher-0004|P12|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-15-goal","e2e-16-constant-floor","e2e-17-no-lowest-score","e2e-18-adversarial-gap"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":4,"subject":"Aligned score is not a literal minimum"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The round-5 index supersedes the frozen round-4 report: it still has $138$ stable steps, but now $68$ are doubly accepted. These comprise researcher-0004 through researcher-0008, including all R7 P1–P12 and R8 [P1]–[P12]. Thus R7 P10 is now the lowest doubly accepted acceptance-driven theorem, at $359229046020947/10^{15}$. This closes the exact source node `e2e-14-source-soundness`; it does not furnish an exact source step for the lower same-cell corollary `e2e-15-goal`.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:20:12Z","id":"msg-8e6d486e9f3b","in_reply_to":"msg-b1bdc086542c","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0008|[P12]|ac8372242c10b8ddcbed8ed8de0d87eaa1c155c1d77a723131c437583007bac5"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-14-source-soundness","e2e-14-numeric-agreement","e2e-15-goal"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":5,"subject":"Round-5 evidence boundary"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The R7 source cell is now anchored by an accepted theorem. The remaining arithmetic deduction is $$k_7=1151782755825594=\\lceil N\\varepsilon_7\\rceil,$$ $$\\frac{k_7-1}{N}<0.3592290460209469<\\varepsilon_7,$$ with cleared lower inequality $1890605983883898>0$. Please retain `cc-aligned-rounding` as a separate exact-statement obligation: the accepted R7 hash proves the endpoint theorem, not this cell extension.","channel":"certified-computation","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:20:12Z","id":"msg-c2f8764fd9f1","in_reply_to":"msg-21f0ad2d7db4","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["certified-computation/cc-aligned-rounding","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-14-source-soundness","e2e-14-numeric-agreement","e2e-15-goal"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":5,"subject":"Keep source-cell alignment separate"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The new R7 accepts remain fixed-score and source-core specific. Lowering the accepted count to $k_+=1151782755825593$ still requires hypothesis-parametric versions of P2 and P6 and transfer of P8–P9 to the new core. Please audit `e2e-21-one-edge-obligation` only in that strengthened form. R7 P12 also confirms that the point-degree envelope is sharp at the incidence-graph level, so further improvement must exploit line-side or label structure.","channel":"exact-analytic","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:20:12Z","id":"msg-162230010291","in_reply_to":"msg-6e54b12e8617","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P6|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P8|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P9|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P12|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-20-point-degree-barrier","e2e-21-one-edge-obligation"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":5,"subject":"One-edge refinement remains new"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The literal optimization still has no positive minimizer: accepted constant-polynomial evidence gives every rational $0<\\varepsilon\\le10/147457$, while the accepted adversarial construction refutes $[20/147457,88/147457]$. Accordingly, $0.3592290460209469$ is only a concrete acceptance-driven source-cell representative, not the lowest member of the formal sound-score set.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:20:12Z","id":"msg-f33142048ba1","in_reply_to":"msg-03581cb32eba","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["researcher-0005|P19|f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","researcher-0004|P12|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-15-goal","e2e-16-constant-floor","e2e-17-no-lowest-score","e2e-18-adversarial-gap"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":5,"subject":"No literal lowest score"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"The live round-5 index supersedes the frozen R6 report: it has $138$ stable steps and $68$ double accepts, namely every step of researchers 0004--0008. R7 P10 is now the best accepted acceptance-driven source theorem at $359229046020947/10^{15}$; R8 is also accepted but numerically dominated.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:20:12Z","id":"msg-a4b109219a49","in_reply_to":"msg-65d0f85325c4","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0008|[P12]|ac8372242c10b8ddcbed8ed8de0d87eaa1c155c1d77a723131c437583007bac5"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r7-source-theorem","cc-r7-source-cell","cc-frontier-cells"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":5,"subject":"Round-5 trust boundary includes R7 and R8"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"The accepted R7 source value has $(k_7,r_7)=(1151782755825594,781092077)$ and residue $922933$. Exact rounding therefore makes the whole cell sound; $0.3592290460209469$ is inside because $3592290460209469N-10^{16}(k_7-1)=1890605983883898>0$. This cell corollary is derived, not itself the audited theorem hash.","channel":"end-to-end-soundness","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:20:12Z","id":"msg-bbe7290b676a","in_reply_to":"msg-21f0ad2d7db4","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","certified-computation/cc-r7-source-cell"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r7-arithmetic-ledger","cc-r7-source-theorem","cc-r7-source-cell"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":5,"subject":"R7 ledger and source cell now rest on accepted ancestry"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"Now that R7 is accepted, please remove fixed-score P2/P6/P8/P9 evidence_refs from every strengthened one-edge node. Those hashes state hypotheses at $\\varepsilon_7$, not at $k_+/N$. In this roadmap, `cc-r7-parametric-bridge` and `cc-r7-one-edge-cell` deliberately have empty evidence_refs until the generic envelope, core, component-mass, and recovery interfaces are independently indexed.","channel":"exact-analytic","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:20:12Z","id":"msg-e0c9916df822","in_reply_to":"msg-4600448b4715","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P6|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P8|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P9|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r7-one-edge-arithmetic","cc-r7-parametric-bridge","cc-r7-one-edge-cell"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":5,"subject":"Prevent accepted hashes from promoting stronger generic statements"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"The R7 note contains a manifest-bound integer/Fraction checker, and both auditors report rerunning it successfully; this closes the displayed scalar ledger only. It is not a canonical `BadIP` instance, generator-refinement proof, complete outer family, or UNSAT proof. The direct one-edge certificate boundary therefore remains open.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:20:12Z","id":"msg-843be9c50811","in_reply_to":"msg-8a9b45c2da0e","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/submissions/researcher-0007/manifest.json","research_state/campaign-10-ultra/submissions/researcher-0007/note.md","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r7-arithmetic-ledger","cc-proof-checker","cc-generator-refinement","cc-certificate-schema","cc-r7-direct-artifact"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":5,"subject":"Scalar checker exists; direct finite UNSAT artifact does not"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"The current snapshot has $138$ stable steps and $68$ double-accepted steps. All R7 and R8 steps are now double accepted, so `ea-50-r7-source-soundness` at $359229046020947/10^{15}$ replaces the old R6 baseline. R8 is accepted but numerically weaker.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:20:12Z","id":"msg-f380ef1e8293","in_reply_to":"msg-3ebc75f0b62d","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0008|[P12]|ac8372242c10b8ddcbed8ed8de0d87eaa1c155c1d77a723131c437583007bac5"],"related_node_ids":["ea-50-r7-source-soundness","ea-59-r8-accepted-comparison"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":5,"subject":"Round-5 trust update"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"Please certify the exact source cell in `ea-51-r7-source-cell` and the tightened endpoint calculations in `ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints`. The accepted R7 theorem gives the full cell containing $0.35922904602094685$. Replaying P2 with $h_j^*=2387626371315326/10^{16}$ and $h_P^*=170031583622226/10^{16}$ gives a positive survival margin at $k_2=1151782755825592$ and a negative margin at $k_2-1$, yielding the provisional score $0.3592290460209463$.","channel":"certified-computation","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:20:12Z","id":"msg-85802156fbbf","in_reply_to":"msg-b97e12db4201","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["ea-51-r7-source-cell","ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints","ea-64-r7-two-incidence-core","ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":5,"subject":"Certify the source cell and two-incidence arithmetic"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"R7/P8 and P9 are now accepted for the exact P6 core, but the two-incidence route still needs their hypothesis-parametric forms. Please audit `ea-56-r7-generic-mass` and `ea-57-r7-generic-recovery` for an arbitrary core having the displayed minimum degrees, formal $B$-identities, and pointwise simple roots.","channel":"end-to-end-soundness","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:20:12Z","id":"msg-d695a051ce00","in_reply_to":"msg-6e54b12e8617","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0007|P8|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P9|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["ea-56-r7-generic-mass","ea-57-r7-generic-recovery","ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":5,"subject":"Audit generic component recovery"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"Do not promote $0.3592290460209463$ merely because R7/P2, P6, P8, and P9 are now accepted. Their indexed statements remain fixed-score or source-core-specific. The tightened endpoint bounds, acceptance-parametric energy lemma, generic ledger, and generic component transfers require exact matching sources and audits.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:20:12Z","id":"msg-e251867cdc13","in_reply_to":"msg-4600448b4715","informal":true,"kind":"objection","references":["researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P6|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P8|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P9|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["ea-52-r7-envelope-certificate","ea-53-r7-parametric-energy","ea-54-r7-generic-ledger","ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints","ea-63-r7-tight-parametric-energy","ea-64-r7-two-incidence-core","ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":5,"subject":"Keep the tightened frontier provisional"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"The round-6 snapshot has $138$ stable steps and $68$ double accepts. Its sole corpus addition is the Lemma Book extraction for researcher-0010; R10 remains `revise,revise` and is numerically weaker than R7. Thus R7 P10 remains the best doubly accepted acceptance-driven theorem.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z","id":"msg-55c944736dcb","in_reply_to":"msg-a4b109219a49","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0010|P10|a011600739e25d4ffa0074a86b31b5861524f97eb2ef11ef1a68fd711533c8a2"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r7-source-theorem","cc-r7-source-cell","cc-exact-score-set"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":6,"subject":"Round-6 evidence boundary"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"Exact replay gives the tightened endpoint ceilings and the positive $k_2$ margin $$\\frac{24329817599601268271}{383232578610782139852500000000000000}>0,$$ while the neighboring margin is negative. Hence the scalar machinery gains exactly two incidences. The endpoint certificate and the generic P2/P6/P8/P9 interfaces still lack matching stable evidence, so $0.3592290460209463$ remains blocked.","channel":"exact-analytic","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z","id":"msg-cadc9ebd32cc","in_reply_to":"msg-85802156fbbf","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["exact-analytic/ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints","exact-analytic/ea-63-r7-tight-parametric-energy","exact-analytic/ea-64-r7-two-incidence-core","exact-analytic/ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r7-tight-endpoints","cc-r7-envelope-certificate","cc-r7-parametric-energy","cc-r7-two-incidence-arithmetic","cc-r7-generic-core","cc-r7-generic-mass","cc-r7-generic-recovery","cc-r7-two-incidence-cell"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":6,"subject":"Two-incidence arithmetic is exact but provisional"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"The accepted P10 theorem and integer-cell lemma are kept separate. They give the full source cell $$\\left(\\frac{1151782755825593}{N},\\frac{1151782755825594}{N}\\right],$$ containing $0.35922904602094685$ because the cleared lower surplus is $2874745436739770>0$. This representative is derived, not part of the P10 hash.","channel":"end-to-end-soundness","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z","id":"msg-bf4faf8d0398","in_reply_to":"msg-c2f8764fd9f1","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","certified-computation/cc-aligned-rounding","certified-computation/cc-r7-source-cell"],"related_node_ids":["cc-aligned-rounding","cc-r7-source-theorem","cc-r7-source-cell"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":6,"subject":"Exact R7 source-cell separation"},{"author":"certified-computation","body_markdown":"The direct target is now $\\operatorname{BadIP}(1151782755825592,781092077)$. No canonical generated formula, semantic refinement proof, complete line-side outer family, hash-bound UNSAT proof, or accepting kernel run exists. The accepted R7 scalar checker does not close this obligation.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z","id":"msg-aef431c0ffc5","in_reply_to":"msg-843be9c50811","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["certified-computation/cc-proof-checker","certified-computation/cc-generator-refinement","certified-computation/cc-outer-relaxation","certified-computation/cc-r7-direct-artifact"],"related_node_ids":["cc-proof-checker","cc-generator-refinement","cc-certificate-schema","cc-degree-sequence-limit","cc-outer-relaxation","cc-r7-direct-artifact"],"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":6,"subject":"Retarget direct UNSAT certification to two incidences"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"The refreshed corpus still has $138$ stable steps and $68$ double accepts. R7 remains the lowest accepted acceptance-driven theorem at $359229046020947/10^{15}$. R9 is unaudited, while R10 remains `revise/revise` and its score $638436441892593/1603131440209921$ is larger than R7.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z","id":"msg-eca09646323b","in_reply_to":"msg-f380ef1e8293","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0010|P10|a011600739e25d4ffa0074a86b31b5861524f97eb2ef11ef1a68fd711533c8a2"],"related_node_ids":["ea-50-r7-source-soundness","ea-59-r8-accepted-comparison","ea-60-r10-revised-fallback"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":6,"subject":"Round-6 trust and frontier update"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"Please certify `ea-51-r7-source-cell`, `ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints`, and the exact arithmetic in `ea-64-r7-two-incidence-core`. With $h_j^*=2387626371315326/10^{16}$ and $h_P^*=170031583622226/10^{16}$, the normalized margin is positive at $k_2=1151782755825592$ and negative at $k_2-1$. Thus this endpoint certificate gains exactly two incidences and places $0.3592290460209463$ in the candidate cell.","channel":"certified-computation","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z","id":"msg-248da7ceae0e","in_reply_to":"msg-85802156fbbf","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["certified-computation/cc-aligned-rounding","researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["ea-51-r7-source-cell","ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints","ea-63-r7-tight-parametric-energy","ea-64-r7-two-incidence-core","ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":6,"subject":"Certify the source cell and two-incidence arithmetic"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"Please audit `ea-56-r7-generic-mass` and `ea-57-r7-generic-recovery` in their displayed hypothesis-parametric forms. The mass proof should use only affine mixing and minimum degrees $(17643,5495)$. Recovery should assume the primitive squarefree $B$-identities, pointwise $B_Z\\ne0$, point degree at least $D+1$, and connectedness.","channel":"end-to-end-soundness","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z","id":"msg-dc91ab904939","in_reply_to":"msg-d695a051ce00","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0007|P7|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P8|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P9|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["ea-23-formal-implicit","ea-56-r7-generic-mass","ea-57-r7-generic-recovery","ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":6,"subject":"Audit generic mass and recovery"},{"author":"exact-analytic","body_markdown":"R7/P2's proof explicitly contains the global chord calculation, but no accepted source step states the tightened endpoints or the resulting $A$-parametric bound. Likewise P6, P8, and P9 remain source-core-specific. Do not promote the $k_2$ interval until the strengthened endpoint, ledger, mass, and recovery statements receive exact matching evidence.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z","id":"msg-10747c774fc3","in_reply_to":"msg-e251867cdc13","informal":true,"kind":"objection","references":["researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P6|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P8|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P9|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["ea-52-r7-envelope-certificate","ea-54-r7-generic-ledger","ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints","ea-63-r7-tight-parametric-energy","ea-56-r7-generic-mass","ea-57-r7-generic-recovery","ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness"],"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":6,"subject":"Keep strengthened R7 interfaces separate"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The round-6 snapshot has $138$ stable steps and $68$ double accepts, exactly from researchers 0004--0008. R7 P10 remains the lowest accepted acceptance-driven source theorem. R9 P13 has no audits, while R10 is `revise, revise` and numerically weaker than R7; neither changes the accepted frontier.","channel":"global","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z","id":"msg-af43e12db944","in_reply_to":"msg-8e6d486e9f3b","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0009|P13|da89baf01629f789c4e9b56d186509a33896212a6b7f0f105aedf3431f4d8b03","researcher-0010|P10|a011600739e25d4ffa0074a86b31b5861524f97eb2ef11ef1a68fd711533c8a2"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-14-source-soundness","e2e-15-goal","e2e-28-pencil-gap-extension"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":6,"subject":"Round-6 evidence boundary"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"Joint acceptance and recovery integrality extends R7 P10 to the whole cell, not merely to $\\varepsilon\\le\\varepsilon_7$. With $C=1474580$, $$k_7-1=781092077C+922933,$$ so the source conclusion forces $781092078$ agreement points, enough throughout $$\\frac{k_7-1}{N}<\\varepsilon\\le\\frac{k_7}{N}.$$ The terminating value $0.35922904602094685$ lies in this cell. This deduction remains separate from the P10 evidence triple.","channel":"certified-computation","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z","id":"msg-781b1200a647","in_reply_to":"msg-bbe7290b676a","informal":true,"kind":"reply","references":["certified-computation/cc-r7-source-cell","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-14-source-soundness","e2e-14-numeric-agreement","e2e-15-goal"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":6,"subject":"Use the full joint count cell"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"The proposed $k_2=1151782755825592$ refinement still requires hypothesis-parametric energy, a score-independent core ledger, generic component mass, and generic recovery. Nodes `e2e-22-parametric-energy` through `e2e-27-two-incidence-frontier` therefore retain empty evidence references: accepted R7 P2, P6, P8, and P9 state only the fixed source regime.","channel":"exact-analytic","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z","id":"msg-db6125b2a76b","in_reply_to":"msg-d695a051ce00","informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["exact-analytic/ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints","exact-analytic/ea-63-r7-tight-parametric-energy","exact-analytic/ea-54-r7-generic-ledger","exact-analytic/ea-56-r7-generic-mass","exact-analytic/ea-57-r7-generic-recovery"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-22-parametric-energy","e2e-23-generic-ledger","e2e-24-generic-component-mass","e2e-25-generic-recovery","e2e-27-two-incidence-frontier"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":6,"subject":"Audit the two-incidence interfaces"},{"author":"end-to-end-soundness","body_markdown":"Please audit researcher-0009 P13 independently. It claims a table with $$\\operatorname{Pass}\\ge\\frac{13123585}{21743566849},\\qquad \\operatorname{Agr}_{87}<\\frac6{147457},$$ extending the known nonsound interval to $[20/147457,13123585/21743566849]$ when combined with R4 P12. The claim currently has no verifier verdict.","channel":"exact-analytic","created_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z","id":"msg-ad847ba94752","in_reply_to":null,"informal":true,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0009|P13|da89baf01629f789c4e9b56d186509a33896212a6b7f0f105aedf3431f4d8b03","researcher-0004|P12|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-18-adversarial-gap","e2e-28-pencil-gap-extension"],"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":6,"subject":"Audit the R9 pencil obstruction"}],"schema":"line-point-roadmap-message-board-v1","updated_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z"},"proof_roadmaps":{"active_roadmaps":[],"model":"gpt-5.6-sol","reasoning_effort":"ultra","roadmaps":[{"corpus_sha256":"ea74c83b4a458f21070007b5661f3dc825852d26afbb96773d309aa1f3e16ed5","critical_path":["ea-00-prime-certificate","ea-01-fixed-instance","ea-02-score-set","ea-03-constant-floor","ea-04-no-least-score","ea-80-round6-conclusion"],"focus":"constant-optimized pruning, interpolation, factorization, and one-polynomial recovery","goal_node_id":"ea-80-round6-conclusion","messages":[{"body_markdown":"The refreshed corpus still has $138$ stable steps and $68$ double accepts. R7 remains the lowest accepted acceptance-driven theorem at $359229046020947/10^{15}$. R9 is unaudited, while R10 remains `revise/revise` and its score $638436441892593/1603131440209921$ is larger than R7.","channel":"global","in_reply_to":"msg-f380ef1e8293","kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0010|P10|a011600739e25d4ffa0074a86b31b5861524f97eb2ef11ef1a68fd711533c8a2"],"related_node_ids":["ea-50-r7-source-soundness","ea-59-r8-accepted-comparison","ea-60-r10-revised-fallback"],"subject":"Round-6 trust and frontier update"},{"body_markdown":"Please certify `ea-51-r7-source-cell`, `ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints`, and the exact arithmetic in `ea-64-r7-two-incidence-core`. With $h_j^*=2387626371315326/10^{16}$ and $h_P^*=170031583622226/10^{16}$, the normalized margin is positive at $k_2=1151782755825592$ and negative at $k_2-1$. Thus this endpoint certificate gains exactly two incidences and places $0.3592290460209463$ in the candidate cell.","channel":"certified-computation","in_reply_to":"msg-85802156fbbf","kind":"request","references":["certified-computation/cc-aligned-rounding","researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["ea-51-r7-source-cell","ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints","ea-63-r7-tight-parametric-energy","ea-64-r7-two-incidence-core","ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness"],"subject":"Certify the source cell and two-incidence arithmetic"},{"body_markdown":"Please audit `ea-56-r7-generic-mass` and `ea-57-r7-generic-recovery` in their displayed hypothesis-parametric forms. The mass proof should use only affine mixing and minimum degrees $(17643,5495)$. Recovery should assume the primitive squarefree $B$-identities, pointwise $B_Z\\ne0$, point degree at least $D+1$, and connectedness.","channel":"end-to-end-soundness","in_reply_to":"msg-d695a051ce00","kind":"request","references":["researcher-0007|P7|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P8|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P9|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["ea-23-formal-implicit","ea-56-r7-generic-mass","ea-57-r7-generic-recovery","ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness"],"subject":"Audit generic mass and recovery"},{"body_markdown":"R7/P2's proof explicitly contains the global chord calculation, but no accepted source step states the tightened endpoints or the resulting $A$-parametric bound. Likewise P6, P8, and P9 remain source-core-specific. Do not promote the $k_2$ interval until the strengthened endpoint, ledger, mass, and recovery statements receive exact matching evidence.","channel":"global","in_reply_to":"msg-e251867cdc13","kind":"objection","references":["researcher-0007|P2|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P6|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P8|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0007|P9|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["ea-52-r7-envelope-certificate","ea-54-r7-generic-ledger","ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints","ea-63-r7-tight-parametric-energy","ea-56-r7-generic-mass","ea-57-r7-generic-recovery","ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness"],"subject":"Keep strengthened R7 interfaces separate"}],"nodes":[{"dependencies":[],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P1"}],"id":"ea-00-prime-certificate","kind":"lemma","label":"Fixed-prime certificate","notes":"Accepted exact certificate for the fixed field.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P1.1"],"statement_markdown":"For $p=147457$, $p-1=2^{14}3^2$ and the Lucas congruences recorded in R7/P1 certify that $p$ is prime.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-00-prime-certificate"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-01-fixed-instance","kind":"definition","label":"Fixed affine-plane protocol","notes":"All probabilities use uniform affine-line-then-uniform-point sampling.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $F=\\mathbb F_{147457}$, $d=87$, $\\mathcal P=F^2$, and $\\mathcal L$ be the affine lines. Then $$M=|\\mathcal P|=21743566849,\\quad \\Lambda=|\\mathcal L|=21743714306,\\quad N=M(p+1)=3206262880419842.$$ For a point table $f$ and degree-at-most-$87$ line labels $P_L$, let $A_{\\rm acc}$ be the accepted-incidence count, $\\operatorname{Pass}=A_{\\rm acc}/N$, and let $G(f)$ be the largest number of points on which $f$ agrees with one total-degree-at-most-$87$ polynomial. Put $\\operatorname{Agr}_{87}(f)=G(f)/M$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-01-fixed-instance"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-02-score-set","kind":"definition","label":"Sound-score set","notes":"The predicate need not be monotone because its required agreement changes with the score.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Define $$\\operatorname{Sound}(\\varepsilon)\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall(f,P),\\quad \\operatorname{Pass}(f,P)\\ge\\varepsilon\\Longrightarrow\\operatorname{Agr}_{87}(f)\\ge\\varepsilon/10,$$ and $$\\mathcal S=\\{\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb Q:0<\\varepsilon\\le1\\text{ and }\\operatorname{Sound}(\\varepsilon)\\}.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-02-score-set"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0004","source_response_sha256":"d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","source_step_id":"P15"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0005","source_response_sha256":"f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","source_step_id":"P19"}],"id":"ea-03-constant-floor","kind":"lemma","label":"Universal constant-polynomial floor","notes":"Both exact sources are double accepted.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0004:P15.1","researcher-0005:P19.1"],"statement_markdown":"Every $f:\\mathcal P\\to F$ has a fiber of size at least $p$. Hence some constant polynomial agrees with $f$ on density at least $1/p$, and $$(0,10/147457]\\cap\\mathbb Q\\subseteq\\mathcal S.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-03-constant-floor"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-04-no-least-score","kind":"theorem","label":"No lowest positive score","notes":"This resolves the target as literally stated.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"The rational sound-score set $\\mathcal S$ has infimum $0$ and no least element. The same holds after restricting to positive terminating decimals.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-02-score-set"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0004","source_response_sha256":"d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","source_step_id":"P12"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0005","source_response_sha256":"f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","source_step_id":"P18"}],"id":"ea-05-score-gap","kind":"theorem","label":"Accepted nonmonotonicity obstruction","notes":"This forbids treating an accepted endpoint as the start of a monotone interval.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0004:P12.1","researcher-0005:P18.1"],"statement_markdown":"There are tables with $$\\operatorname{Pass}(f,P)\\ge\\frac{88}{147457},\\qquad \\operatorname{Agr}_{87}(f)<\\frac2{147457}.$$ Therefore $[20/147457,88/147457]\\cap\\mathbb Q$ is disjoint from $\\mathcal S$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-02-score-set"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-07-integer-cells","kind":"reduction","label":"Exact acceptance and recovery cells","notes":"Elementary integer rounding; the corresponding computational-roadmap lemma is `cc-aligned-rounding`.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Put $H=10(p+1)=1474580$. For $0<\\varepsilon\\le1$, set $$k=\\lceil N\\varepsilon\\rceil,\\qquad r_k=\\left\\lfloor\\frac{k-1}{H}\\right\\rfloor.$$ Then $$\\neg\\operatorname{Sound}(\\varepsilon)\\Longleftrightarrow\\exists(f,P):\\ A_{\\rm acc}\\ge k\\text{ and }G(f)\\le r_k.$$ Hence soundness is constant on each cell $((k-1)/N,k/N]$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-01-fixed-instance"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P7"}],"id":"ea-10-centered-mixing","kind":"lemma","label":"Exact centered affine mixing","notes":"Universal for every point-line subgraph.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P7.1"],"statement_markdown":"For $X\\subseteq\\mathcal P$ and $T\\subseteq\\mathcal L$, let $a=|X|/M$, $b=|T|/\\Lambda$, and $J=I(X,T)/N$. Then $$|J-ab|\\le\\sqrt{\\frac{a(1-a)b(1-b)}{p+1}}.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-01-fixed-instance"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P1"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P2"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P6"}],"id":"ea-42-r7-parameters","kind":"definition","label":"R7 exact parameter ledger","notes":"Fixed constants for both the accepted source proof and the two-incidence refinement.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P1.1","researcher-0007:P2.1","researcher-0007:P6.1"],"statement_markdown":"Set $$P_0=147458,\\quad \\varepsilon_7=\\frac{359229046020947}{10^{15}},\\quad \\tau_7=\\frac{\\varepsilon_7}{10},$$ $$D=17642,\\quad r=600782,\\quad s=5495,\\quad j=51837,\\quad q=17555.$$ Then $$V_D=10599598107>r(D+1)=10599596826,\\quad E_D=3559710,$$ and $$C_0=Dp^2+(q+s-1)\\Lambda+(p-q-s+1)E_D=885213733790732.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-42-r7-parameters"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-23-formal-implicit","kind":"literature_input","label":"Simple-root lifting interface","notes":"Required generic form of KTZ Lemmas 2.5, 2.7, and 6.1; R7/P9 audits only their exact source-core application.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $B\\in F[X,Y,Z]$ have $(1,1,87)$-weighted degree at most $D$. If $D+1$ distinct lines through $x$ carry degree-at-most-$87$ polynomial roots of $B$ with a common simple value, then one $Q\\in F[X,Y]$ of total degree at most $87$ satisfies $B(X,Y,Q)=0$ and restricts to every seed-line root. On a line, two degree-at-most-$87$ roots agreeing at a simple value are identical.","work_state":"open"},{"dependencies":["ea-42-r7-parameters"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P2"}],"id":"ea-43-r7-pencil-energy","kind":"lemma","label":"Accepted fixed-score whole-pencil energy","notes":"Exact fixed-score source statement.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P2.1"],"statement_markdown":"For $0\\le a\\le P_0$, put $$H_a=\\frac{\\binom{\\Lambda-a}{r}}{\\binom{\\Lambda}{r}},\\qquad \\phi_a=aH_a.$$ Let $$h_j=\\frac{238762637131533}{10^{15}},\\qquad h_P=\\frac{17003158362223}{10^{15}},$$ $$\\Delta_7=\\frac{j(1-\\varepsilon_7)h_j+(P_0\\varepsilon_7-j)h_P}{P_0-j}.$$ If $|E|/N\\ge\\varepsilon_7$, some $r$-line set $R$ satisfies $U_R/N<\\Delta_7$, where $U_R$ counts accepted incidences whose point's accepted pencil misses $R$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-42-r7-parameters"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P3"}],"id":"ea-44-r7-interpolant","kind":"lemma","label":"Squarefree weighted interpolant","notes":"Minimum weighted degree ranges over all eligible nonzero relations with nonzero $Z$-derivative.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P3.1"],"statement_markdown":"For every $r$-line set $R$, there is a nonzero squarefree $\\mathscr A\\in F[X,Y,Z]$ with $$\\operatorname{wdeg}_{(1,1,87)}\\mathscr A\\le D,\\quad \\mathscr A_Z\\ne0,\\quad \\deg_Z\\mathscr A\\le202<p,$$ such that $\\mathscr A(L(t),P_L(t))\\equiv0$ for every $L\\in R$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-44-r7-interpolant"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P4"}],"id":"ea-45-r7-identity-lines","kind":"reduction","label":"Mass-preserving identity-line extension","notes":"Transfers the relation without imposing a separate popularity threshold.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P4.1"],"statement_markdown":"Let $T$ contain $R$ and every other line having more than $D$ accepted points whose accepted pencils meet $R$. Every $L\\in T$ satisfies $\\mathscr A(L(t),P_L(t))\\equiv0$, and $$|E|\\le |E_T|+U_R+D(\\Lambda-|T|).$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-44-r7-interpolant","ea-45-r7-identity-lines"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P5"}],"id":"ea-46-r7-primitive-cleanup","kind":"lemma","label":"Primitive nominal-discriminant cleanup","notes":"Nominal-degree homogenization handles leading-coefficient drops without division.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P5.1"],"statement_markdown":"Write $\\mathscr A=CB$ with $C\\in F[X,Y]$ and $B$ primitive. If $W=\\operatorname{wdeg}B$ and $\\nu=\\deg_ZB$, then $$1\\le\\nu\\le202<p,\\qquad \\gcd(B,B_Z)=1.$$ At most $E_D=3559710$ identity lines are content- or derivative-degenerate. On every other identity line, $B_Z(L(t),P_L(t))$ is nonzero of degree at most $q=17555$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-43-r7-pencil-energy","ea-45-r7-identity-lines","ea-46-r7-primitive-cleanup"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P6"}],"id":"ea-47-r7-source-core","kind":"reduction","label":"Accepted R7 simple-root core","notes":"This exact conclusion is specialized to the source score $\\varepsilon_7$.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P6.1"],"statement_markdown":"The exact margin $$\\varepsilon_7-\\frac{C_0}{N}-\\Delta_7=\\frac{67333805766276738068309588974841569}{153293031444312855941000000000000000000000000000000}>0$$ leaves a nonempty core of minimum point and line degrees $(17643,5495)$. Every retained line carries a formal $B$-identity, and every retained point $x$ satisfies $$B(x,f(x))=0,\\qquad B_Z(x,f(x))\\ne0.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-42-r7-parameters"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P8"}],"id":"ea-68-r7-component-certificate","kind":"lemma","label":"Exact component scalar certificate","notes":"Arithmetic sublemma displayed inside accepted R7/P8.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P8.1"],"statement_markdown":"Let $$\\alpha=\\frac{17643}{147458},\\quad \\beta=\\frac{5495}{147457},\\quad c=\\frac\\alpha\\beta,\\quad \\gamma^2=\\frac{5495}{2601583851},$$ and $$F(a)=(\\beta-a)^2-\\gamma^2(1-a)(1-ca).$$ For $\\tau=\\tau_7$, one has $\\beta>\\tau$, $c\\tau<1/2$, $$F(\\tau)=\\frac{310822941801540312341284744748980665822691}{5656809599924727240600000000000000000000000000000000}>0,$$ $F'(\\tau)<0$, and $F''=2(1-1/147458)>0$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-10-centered-mixing","ea-47-r7-source-core","ea-68-r7-component-certificate"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P8"}],"id":"ea-48-r7-component-mass","kind":"lemma","label":"Accepted source-component mass","notes":"Exact source-core statement.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P8.1"],"statement_markdown":"Every connected component of the source core has point density greater than $\\tau_7$ and therefore contains at least $781092078$ point vertices.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-46-r7-primitive-cleanup","ea-47-r7-source-core"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P9"}],"id":"ea-49-r7-component-recovery","kind":"lemma","label":"Accepted source-core one-polynomial recovery","notes":"Both audits accepted the KTZ imports in this exact application.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P9.1"],"statement_markdown":"For every connected component $K$ of the source core, there is one $Q_K\\in F[X,Y]$ of total degree at most $87$ such that $Q_K(x)=f(x)$ for every point vertex $x$ of $K$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-02-score-set","ea-48-r7-component-mass","ea-49-r7-component-recovery"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P10"}],"id":"ea-50-r7-source-soundness","kind":"theorem","label":"Accepted R7 analytic soundness","notes":"Lowest double-accepted acceptance-driven source theorem in this corpus.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P10.1"],"statement_markdown":"One has $$\\varepsilon_7=\\frac{359229046020947}{10^{15}}\\in\\mathcal S.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-07-integer-cells","ea-50-r7-source-soundness"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-51-r7-source-cell","kind":"theorem","label":"Full accepted R7 count cell","notes":"An elementary exact corollary, deliberately separated from the accepted endpoint hash.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $$k_7=\\lceil N\\varepsilon_7\\rceil=1151782755825594.$$ Since $$k_7-1=781092077H+922933,$$ one has $$\\left((k_7-1)/N,k_7/N\\right]\\cap\\mathbb Q\\subseteq\\mathcal S.$$ In particular, $$\\varepsilon_7^*=\\frac{35922904602094685}{10^{17}}$$ is sound because $$35922904602094685N-10^{17}(k_7-1)=2874745436739770>0.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-42-r7-parameters"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P2"}],"id":"ea-52-r7-envelope-certificate","kind":"lemma","label":"Global hypergeometric chord certificate","notes":"The global chord is explicit in P2's accepted proof; its tightened endpoint substitution is separated below.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P2.1"],"statement_markdown":"For $$H_a=\\frac{\\binom{\\Lambda-a}{r}}{\\binom{\\Lambda}{r}},\\qquad \\phi_a=aH_a,$$ every integer $0\\le a\\le P_0$ satisfies $$\\phi_a\\le\\frac{(P_0-a)\\phi_j+(a-j)\\phi_{P_0}}{P_0-j}.$$","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["ea-52-r7-envelope-certificate"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints","kind":"lemma","label":"Tightened endpoint probability bounds","notes":"Requires an exact product or even-binomial certificate at the improved rational ceilings.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For $$h_j^*=\\frac{2387626371315326}{10^{16}},\\qquad h_P^*=\\frac{170031583622226}{10^{16}},$$ the exact hypergeometric probabilities satisfy $$H_j<h_j^*,\\qquad H_{P_0}<h_P^*.$$","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["ea-52-r7-envelope-certificate","ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-63-r7-tight-parametric-energy","kind":"lemma","label":"Tight acceptance-parametric energy","notes":"This is the strengthened probabilistic interface needed below $k_7$.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For every accepted graph with $j/P_0\\le A=|E|/N\\le1$, some $r$-line set $R$ satisfies $$\\frac{U_R}{N}<\\Delta_*(A):=\\frac{j(1-A)h_j^*+(P_0A-j)h_P^*}{P_0-j}.$$","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["ea-42-r7-parameters","ea-44-r7-interpolant","ea-45-r7-identity-lines","ea-46-r7-primitive-cleanup"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-54-r7-generic-ledger","kind":"reduction","label":"Hypothesis-parametric interpolation and deletion ledger","notes":"Packages the score-independent content of P3–P6 without importing P6's fixed-score conclusion.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For every $r$-line set $R$, the interpolation, identity transfer, primitive cleanup, and $(D+1,s)$ peel either produce a nonempty core with minimum degrees $(17643,5495)$, formal $B$-identities, and pointwise simple roots, or imply $$|E|\\le U_R+C_0.$$","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["ea-54-r7-generic-ledger","ea-63-r7-tight-parametric-energy"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-64-r7-two-incidence-core","kind":"reduction","label":"Two-incidence optimized core","notes":"The negative neighboring margin limits only this displayed endpoint certificate, not every possible refinement.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $$k_2=1151782755825592,\\qquad A_2=k_2/N.$$ Then $$A_2-\\frac{C_0}{N}-\\Delta_*(A_2)=\\frac{24329817599601268271}{383232578610782139852500000000000000}>0,$$ while $$\\frac{k_2-1}{N}-\\frac{C_0}{N}-\\Delta_*\\!\\left(\\frac{k_2-1}{N}\\right)=\\frac{-430133165077648103093}{1532930314443128559410000000000000000}<0.$$ The margin is increasing in $A$, so $|E|\\ge k_2$ yields a nonempty invariant-bearing simple-root core.","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["ea-10-centered-mixing","ea-68-r7-component-certificate"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-56-r7-generic-mass","kind":"obligation","label":"Generic component-mass transfer","notes":"The source P8 statement names the P6 core; this abstraction needs its own exact statement.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Every connected component of any affine-incidence subgraph with minimum point and line degrees $(17643,5495)$ has point density greater than $\\tau_7$ and hence at least $781092078$ point vertices.","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["ea-23-formal-implicit"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-57-r7-generic-recovery","kind":"obligation","label":"Generic one-polynomial transfer","notes":"The source P9 statement names the P6 core; this is the required invariant-parametric form.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let a connected incidence component carry a primitive squarefree $B$ of weighted degree at most $D$, degree-at-most-$87$ formal line roots, and point values satisfying $B(x,f(x))=0$ and $B_Z(x,f(x))\\ne0$. If every point has degree at least $D+1$, then one total-degree-at-most-$87$ polynomial $Q$ satisfies $Q(x)=f(x)$ at every point vertex.","work_state":"open"},{"dependencies":["ea-07-integer-cells","ea-56-r7-generic-mass","ea-57-r7-generic-recovery","ea-64-r7-two-incidence-core"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness","kind":"theorem","label":"Two-incidence left-extension interval","notes":"Strongest substantive analytic target; blocked by the displayed generic interfaces.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"blocked","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"One has $$\\left((k_2-1)/N,(k_7-1)/N\\right]\\cap\\mathbb Q\\subseteq\\mathcal S.$$ In particular, $$\\widehat\\varepsilon_2=\\frac{3592290460209463}{10^{16}}$$ is sound because $$3592290460209463N-10^{16}(k_2-1)=2653028701364846>0,$$ $$10^{16}k_2-3592290460209463N=7346971298635154>0,$$ and the required agreement count is $781092078$.","work_state":"blocked"},{"dependencies":["ea-01-fixed-instance","ea-42-r7-parameters"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P11"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P12"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0005","source_response_sha256":"f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","source_step_id":"P16"}],"id":"ea-66-architecture-barriers","kind":"lemma","label":"Pruning and recovery barriers","notes":"Explains why further progress must exploit line labels and retained simple roots.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0005:P16.1","researcher-0007:P11.1","researcher-0007:P12.1"],"statement_markdown":"The affine incidence graph is $K_{2,2}$-free, and every point-degree sequence with entries in $[0,p+1]$ is realizable by an incidence subgraph. Moreover, when $B_Z\\ne0$ is omitted, $B=Z^2-X^2$ admits incompatible polynomial line roots through a common point.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-66-architecture-barriers"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0009","source_response_sha256":"da89baf01629f789c4e9b56d186509a33896212a6b7f0f105aedf3431f4d8b03","source_step_id":"P10"}],"id":"ea-67-r9-singular-pencil","kind":"lemma","label":"Unaudited stronger singular-pencil barrier","notes":"Useful R9 ancestry only; it has no verifier verdicts.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"provisional","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0009:P10.1"],"statement_markdown":"The primitive irreducible squarefree relation $B=Z^2-XY$ has $73730$ concurrent degree-one polynomial line roots through the origin but no polynomial global root. Thus abundance of line roots cannot replace pointwise simplicity.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-02-score-set"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0008","source_response_sha256":"ac8372242c10b8ddcbed8ed8de0d87eaa1c155c1d77a723131c437583007bac5","source_step_id":"[P12]"}],"id":"ea-59-r8-accepted-comparison","kind":"theorem","label":"Accepted R8 comparison theorem","notes":"Double accepted but numerically dominated by R7.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0008:[P12].1"],"statement_markdown":"For $$\\varepsilon_8=\\frac{40002010696871}{10^{14}},$$ acceptance at least $\\varepsilon_8$ forces agreement greater than $\\varepsilon_8/10$ with one total-degree-at-most-$87$ polynomial.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["ea-02-score-set"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0010","source_response_sha256":"a011600739e25d4ffa0074a86b31b5861524f97eb2ef11ef1a68fd711533c8a2","source_step_id":"P10"}],"id":"ea-60-r10-revised-fallback","kind":"theorem","label":"R10 revised geometric-amortized fallback","notes":"Both audits returned `revise`; the score is also strictly larger than R7.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"blocked","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0010:P10.1"],"statement_markdown":"R10 claims soundness at $$\\varepsilon_{10}=\\frac{638436441892593}{1603131440209921}\\approx0.3982433541500461.$$ It is dominated exactly because $$\\varepsilon_{10}-\\varepsilon_7=\\frac{62545063979796245156556784813}{1603131440209921\\cdot10^{15}}>0.$$","work_state":"blocked"},{"dependencies":["ea-04-no-least-score","ea-51-r7-source-cell","ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"ea-80-round6-conclusion","kind":"theorem","label":"Round-6 exact analytic conclusion","notes":"The literal conclusion and R7 source cell are closed consequences; the two-incidence left extension remains blocked.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"blocked","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For $p=147457$, $m=2$, and total degree $87$, the rational and terminating-decimal sound-score sets have infimum $0$ and no least positive member. Moreover, with $k_2=1151782755825592$ and $k_7=1151782755825594$, $$\\left((k_2-1)/N,k_7/N\\right]\\cap\\mathbb Q\\subseteq\\mathcal S.$$ In particular, the substantive interval contains $0.3592290460209463$.","work_state":"blocked"}],"progress":{"blocked":2,"invalid":0,"mapped":13,"open":9,"percent":54,"provisional":0,"total":24,"verified":13},"render_validation":{"math_segments":191,"messages":4,"passed":true,"roadmaps":1},"roadmap_id":"exact-analytic","round":6,"summary":"The literal optimization still has no minimizer: double-accepted constant-polynomial evidence makes every rational $0<\\varepsilon\\le10/147457$ sound. The accepted acceptance-driven frontier remains R7 at $\\varepsilon_7=0.359229046020947$; exact count rounding expands it to its full cell and includes $0.35922904602094685$. The optimized R7 replay uses tighter hypergeometric endpoint ceilings and lowers the provisional trigger by two incidences to $k_2=1151782755825592$, placing $0.3592290460209463$ in the candidate cell. Its remaining exact-statement obligations are the tightened endpoints, acceptance-parametric energy, generic deletion ledger, generic component mass, and generic simple-root recovery. R9 is unaudited, R10 remains `revise/revise`, and neither improves R7.","target_statement":"For $p=147457$, $m=2$, and total degree $87$, prove that the literal sound-score set has no least positive rational or terminating-decimal member; close the full accepted R7 count cell; and prove the two-incidence left extension $$\\left((1151782755825592-1)/N,1151782755825594/N\\right]\\cap\\mathbb Q\\subseteq\\mathcal S,$$ including the explicit substantive score $0.3592290460209463$, by completing the tightened pruning, generic interpolation/deletion, component-mass, and one-polynomial recovery interfaces.","title":"Exact analytic chain","updated_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z"},{"corpus_sha256":"ea74c83b4a458f21070007b5661f3dc825852d26afbb96773d309aa1f3e16ed5","critical_path":["cc-prime-certificate","cc-ambient","cc-count-semantics","cc-aligned-rounding","cc-profile-reduction","cc-exact-score-set"],"focus":"integer programs, exhaustive finite reductions, rational arithmetic, and independently checkable certificates","goal_node_id":"cc-exact-score-set","messages":[{"body_markdown":"The round-6 snapshot has $138$ stable steps and $68$ double accepts. Its sole corpus addition is the Lemma Book extraction for researcher-0010; R10 remains `revise,revise` and is numerically weaker than R7. Thus R7 P10 remains the best doubly accepted acceptance-driven theorem.","channel":"global","in_reply_to":"msg-a4b109219a49","kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0010|P10|a011600739e25d4ffa0074a86b31b5861524f97eb2ef11ef1a68fd711533c8a2"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r7-source-theorem","cc-r7-source-cell","cc-exact-score-set"],"subject":"Round-6 evidence boundary"},{"body_markdown":"Exact replay gives the tightened endpoint ceilings and the positive $k_2$ margin $$\\frac{24329817599601268271}{383232578610782139852500000000000000}>0,$$ while the neighboring margin is negative. Hence the scalar machinery gains exactly two incidences. The endpoint certificate and the generic P2/P6/P8/P9 interfaces still lack matching stable evidence, so $0.3592290460209463$ remains blocked.","channel":"exact-analytic","in_reply_to":"msg-85802156fbbf","kind":"reply","references":["exact-analytic/ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints","exact-analytic/ea-63-r7-tight-parametric-energy","exact-analytic/ea-64-r7-two-incidence-core","exact-analytic/ea-65-r7-two-incidence-soundness"],"related_node_ids":["cc-r7-tight-endpoints","cc-r7-envelope-certificate","cc-r7-parametric-energy","cc-r7-two-incidence-arithmetic","cc-r7-generic-core","cc-r7-generic-mass","cc-r7-generic-recovery","cc-r7-two-incidence-cell"],"subject":"Two-incidence arithmetic is exact but provisional"},{"body_markdown":"The accepted P10 theorem and integer-cell lemma are kept separate. They give the full source cell $$\\left(\\frac{1151782755825593}{N},\\frac{1151782755825594}{N}\\right],$$ containing $0.35922904602094685$ because the cleared lower surplus is $2874745436739770>0$. This representative is derived, not part of the P10 hash.","channel":"end-to-end-soundness","in_reply_to":"msg-c2f8764fd9f1","kind":"reply","references":["researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","certified-computation/cc-aligned-rounding","certified-computation/cc-r7-source-cell"],"related_node_ids":["cc-aligned-rounding","cc-r7-source-theorem","cc-r7-source-cell"],"subject":"Exact R7 source-cell separation"},{"body_markdown":"The direct target is now $\\operatorname{BadIP}(1151782755825592,781092077)$. No canonical generated formula, semantic refinement proof, complete line-side outer family, hash-bound UNSAT proof, or accepting kernel run exists. The accepted R7 scalar checker does not close this obligation.","channel":"global","in_reply_to":"msg-843be9c50811","kind":"reply","references":["certified-computation/cc-proof-checker","certified-computation/cc-generator-refinement","certified-computation/cc-outer-relaxation","certified-computation/cc-r7-direct-artifact"],"related_node_ids":["cc-proof-checker","cc-generator-refinement","cc-certificate-schema","cc-degree-sequence-limit","cc-outer-relaxation","cc-r7-direct-artifact"],"subject":"Retarget direct UNSAT certification to two incidences"}],"nodes":[{"dependencies":[],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P1"}],"id":"cc-prime-certificate","kind":"lemma","label":"Exact Pocklington certificate","notes":"Replay the modular powers and gcds using unbounded integers.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P1.1"],"statement_markdown":"For $p=147457$, $$p-1=2^{14}3^2,\\qquad 10^{147456}\\equiv1\\pmod p,$$ $$10^{73728}\\equiv147456\\pmod p,\\qquad 10^{49152}\\equiv78348\\pmod p,$$ and $$\\gcd(147455,p)=\\gcd(78347,p)=1.$$ Hence Pocklington's criterion gives $\\operatorname{Prime}(p)$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-prime-certificate"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P1"}],"id":"cc-ambient","kind":"definition","label":"Fixed finite geometry","notes":"Fix canonical field representatives, affine-line coordinates, incidence enumerations, and monomial order.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P1.1"],"statement_markdown":"Let $F=\\mathbb F_{147457}$, $X=F^2$, $d=87$, and let $\\mathcal L$ be the affine lines of $X$. Put $$M=|X|=21743566849,\\qquad \\Lambda=|\\mathcal L|=21743714306,$$ $$N=|\\{(L,x):x\\in L\\}|=3206262880419842,$$ $$H=10(p+1)=1474580,\\qquad s=\\binom{89}{2}=3916.$$ Thus $N=M(p+1)$ and $N/H=M/10$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-ambient"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-count-semantics","kind":"definition","label":"Integer acceptance and recovery semantics","notes":"All probabilities are henceforth represented by exact integer counts.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For $c=(f,(P_L)_{L\\in\\mathcal L})$, with $f:X\\to F$ and $\\deg P_L\\le87$, define $$A(c)=|\\{(L,x):x\\in L,\\ P_L(x)=f(x)\\}|,$$ $$G(f)=\\max_{\\deg_{\\mathrm{tot}}Q\\le87}|\\{x\\in X:Q(x)=f(x)\\}|.$$ Then $\\operatorname{Pass}(c)=A(c)/N$, $\\operatorname{Agr}_{87}(f)=G(f)/M$, and $$\\operatorname{Sound}(\\varepsilon)\\Longleftrightarrow\\forall c,\\quad A(c)/N\\ge\\varepsilon\\Longrightarrow G(f)/M\\ge\\varepsilon/10.$$ Let $$\\mathcal S=\\{\\varepsilon\\in\\mathbb Q:0<\\varepsilon\\le1\\ \\land\\ \\operatorname{Sound}(\\varepsilon)\\}.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-count-semantics"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-aligned-rounding","kind":"reduction","label":"Exact integer score cells","notes":"The strict failed-recovery inequality forces the open left endpoint.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For $0<\\varepsilon\\le1$, set $$k=\\lceil N\\varepsilon\\rceil,\\qquad r_k=\\left\\lfloor\\frac{k-1}{H}\\right\\rfloor.$$ Then $$\\left\\lceil\\frac{M\\varepsilon}{10}\\right\\rceil=r_k+1$$ and $$\\neg\\operatorname{Sound}(\\varepsilon)\\Longleftrightarrow\\exists c:\\ A(c)\\ge k\\ \\land\\ G(f)\\le r_k.$$ Consequently, $\\operatorname{Sound}$ is constant on $((k-1)/N,k/N]$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-count-semantics"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-local-line-score","kind":"definition","label":"Local Reed--Solomon score","notes":"Each maximum is finite and uses the canonical line coordinate.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Fix $t_L:F\\to L$ for every line and define $$\\lambda_L(f)=\\max_{\\deg R\\le87}|\\{x\\in L:R(t_L^{-1}(x))=f(x)\\}|,$$ $$T(f)=\\sum_{L\\in\\mathcal L}\\lambda_L(f).$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-local-line-score"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-line-table-elimination","kind":"lemma","label":"Independent line maximization","notes":"Line labels on distinct lines have no compatibility constraint.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For every point table $f$, $$T(f)=\\max_{(P_L)_{L\\in\\mathcal L}}A(f,(P_L)_L).$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-line-table-elimination"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-bad-profile","kind":"definition","label":"Exact bad-instance profile","notes":"The sentinel $-1$ covers an empty constrained family.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For $r\\in\\mathbb Z$, define $$C_r=\\max\\left(\\{-1\\}\\cup\\{T(f):f:X\\to F,\\ G(f)\\le r\\}\\right).$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-aligned-rounding","cc-bad-profile"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-profile-reduction","kind":"reduction","label":"Soundness as one integer inequality","notes":"Equivalently, each table contributes the failure interval $(10G(f)/M,T(f)/N]$.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For $0<\\varepsilon\\le1$, with $k=\\lceil N\\varepsilon\\rceil$ and $r_k=\\lfloor(k-1)/H\\rfloor$, $$\\operatorname{Sound}(\\varepsilon)\\Longleftrightarrow C_{r_k}<k.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-count-semantics"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-bad-ip","kind":"definition","label":"Exact finite bad-instance program","notes":"The program is enormous but finite; every index follows the canonical enumeration in `cc-ambient`.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For integers $k,r$, let $\\operatorname{BadIP}(k,r)$ have binary variables $z_{x,b}$, $u_{L,a}$, and $y_{L,x,b}$, where $b\\in F$ and $a\\in F^{88}$. Impose $$\\sum_bz_{x,b}=1,\\qquad\\sum_au_{L,a}=1.$$ For $R_a(t)=\\sum_{j=0}^{87}a_jt^j$, put $$v_{L,x,b}=\\sum_{a:R_a(t_L^{-1}(x))=b}u_{L,a}$$ and impose $$y_{L,x,b}\\le z_{x,b},\\quad y_{L,x,b}\\le v_{L,x,b},\\quad y_{L,x,b}\\ge z_{x,b}+v_{L,x,b}-1.$$ Finally impose $$\\sum_{L,x\\in L,b}y_{L,x,b}\\ge k$$ and, for every coefficient word $q\\in F^s$ with polynomial $Q_q$, $$\\sum_{x\\in X}z_{x,Q_q(x)}\\le r.$$","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["cc-bad-profile","cc-bad-ip"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-ip-equivalence","kind":"reduction","label":"Integer-program semantics","notes":"The restriction $k\\ge0$ avoids the sentinel counterexample when the $G\\le r$ family is empty.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For every integer $k\\ge0$ and $r\\in\\mathbb Z$, $$\\operatorname{BadIP}(k,r)\\text{ is feasible}\\Longleftrightarrow\\exists c:\\ A(c)\\ge k\\ \\land\\ G(f)\\le r\\Longleftrightarrow C_r\\ge k.$$","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["cc-local-line-score"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-code-coset-compression","kind":"reduction","label":"Reed--Muller coset normalization","notes":"Use the triangular Newton basis to prove the information-set bijection.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $\\mathcal C$ be the evaluation code of total-degree-at-most-$87$ bivariate polynomials and $\\mathcal C_L$ the degree-at-most-$87$ code on $L$. Then $$G(f)=M-d_H(f,\\mathcal C),\\qquad T(f)=N-\\sum_Ld_H(f|_L,\\mathcal C_L).$$ For distinct $\\alpha_0,\\ldots,\\alpha_{87}\\in F$, let $$I=\\{(\\alpha_i,\\alpha_j):i+j\\le87\\}.$$ Evaluation $\\mathcal C\\to F^I$ is bijective, $G$ and $T$ are invariant under $f\\mapsto f+R$ for $R\\in\\mathcal C$, and every coset has a unique representative vanishing on $I$.","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["cc-local-line-score"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-anchor-enumeration","kind":"lemma","label":"Eighty-eight-anchor local enumeration","notes":"This replaces a scan over $p^{88}$ coefficient words by a still-enormous but smaller canonical subset scan.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For every line $L$ and table $f$, one has $\\lambda_L(f)\\ge88$. Every maximizing degree-at-most-$87$ polynomial is determined by some $88$ of its agreement points. Hence $$\\lambda_L(f)=\\max_{\\substack{S\\subseteq L\\\\|S|=88}}|\\{x\\in L:R_S(x)=f(x)\\}|,$$ where $R_S$ is the unique interpolant through $f|_S$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-bad-profile","cc-code-coset-compression","cc-anchor-enumeration"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-exhaustive-profile","kind":"reduction","label":"Finite exhaustive decision procedure","notes":"This establishes decidability, not practical tractability.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Every $C_r$ is determined by enumerating the $$p^{M-s}=p^{21743562933}$$ tables vanishing on $I$. For each representative, scanning $p^{3916}$ global coefficient words computes $G(f)$, while scanning at most $\\Lambda\\binom{p}{88}$ anchored interpolants computes $T(f)$. Thus every predicate $C_r<k$ is an exact finite Boolean obligation.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":[],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-proof-checker","kind":"obligation","label":"Exact proof-checker kernels","notes":"Suitable UNSAT kernels include LRAT, VeriPB, or exhaustive branching with exact nonnegative Farkas leaves.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Canonical parsers and checkers satisfy $$\\operatorname{Check}_{\\mathrm{sat}}(F,w)=\\mathrm{true}\\Longrightarrow\\operatorname{SAT}(F),$$ $$\\operatorname{Check}_{\\mathrm{unsat}}(F,\\pi)=\\mathrm{true}\\Longrightarrow\\neg\\operatorname{SAT}(F),$$ and $$\\operatorname{Check}_{\\mathbb Q}(s,\\alpha)=\\mathrm{true}\\Longrightarrow s$$ for every parsed closed integer-rational proposition $s$. Before parsing referenced bytes, each checker validates manifest lengths and SHA-256 digests.","work_state":"open"},{"dependencies":["cc-bad-ip"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-generator-refinement","kind":"obligation","label":"Deterministic formula generation","notes":"A digest identifies bytes but does not prove semantic refinement.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"A deterministic generator emits canonical pseudo-Boolean or CNF bytes $F_{k,r}$ satisfying $$\\operatorname{SAT}(F_{k,r})\\Longleftrightarrow\\operatorname{BadIP}(k,r)\\text{ is feasible}.$$ The equivalence covers the emitted field, geometry, evaluation, cardinality, and auxiliary-variable encodings.","work_state":"open"},{"dependencies":["cc-aligned-rounding","cc-ip-equivalence","cc-proof-checker","cc-generator-refinement"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-certificate-schema","kind":"theorem","label":"Accepted certificates classify a cell","notes":"This is the small trusted composition theorem; checker and generator soundness remain open.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $1\\le k\\le N$ and $r_k=\\lfloor(k-1)/H\\rfloor$. After generator and manifest validation, $$\\operatorname{Check}_{\\mathrm{unsat}}(F_{k,r_k},\\pi)=\\mathrm{true}$$ implies soundness throughout $((k-1)/N,k/N]$, while $$\\operatorname{Check}_{\\mathrm{sat}}(F_{k,r_k},w)=\\mathrm{true}$$ implies nonsoundness throughout that cell.","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["cc-ambient"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P11"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P12"}],"id":"cc-degree-sequence-limit","kind":"lemma","label":"Point-degree relaxation boundary","notes":"Any useful outer program must add line-side or polynomial-label constraints.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P11.1","researcher-0007:P12.1"],"statement_markdown":"The affine point-line incidence graph is $K_{2,2}$-free, and $$\\{(\\deg_G(x))_{x\\in X}:G\\subseteq\\operatorname{Inc}(X,\\mathcal L)\\}=\\prod_{x\\in X}\\{0,\\ldots,p+1\\}.$$ Thus point-degree histograms alone impose no additional feasibility restriction.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-ip-equivalence","cc-degree-sequence-limit"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-outer-relaxation","kind":"obligation","label":"Explicit finite outer relaxation","notes":"No complete branch family or bad-instance coverage theorem is stored.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"blocked","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For each $(k,r)$ there are a finite set $\\Theta_{k,r}$ and explicit integer systems $\\Phi_\\theta$ such that $$\\operatorname{BadIP}(k,r)\\text{ feasible}\\Longrightarrow\\bigvee_{\\theta\\in\\Theta_{k,r}}\\exists z\\in\\mathbb Z^{s_\\theta}:\\Phi_\\theta(k,r,z).$$ Every branch retains explicit line-side or polynomial-label information, so exact infeasibility certificates for all branches imply infeasibility of $\\operatorname{BadIP}(k,r)$.","work_state":"blocked"},{"dependencies":["cc-ambient"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P1"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P2"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P5"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P6"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P8"}],"id":"cc-r7-arithmetic-ledger","kind":"lemma","label":"Hash-bound R7 rational ledger","notes":"The R7 manifest binds note SHA-256 `8faf0714244fadebd63b29c3c3c4402b36974bc1803bdbdd6402c54f70f293e9`; both auditors reran its integer/Fraction script. This certifies only the displayed scalar ledger.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P1.1","researcher-0007:P2.1","researcher-0007:P5.1","researcher-0007:P6.1","researcher-0007:P8.1"],"statement_markdown":"Let $$\\varepsilon_7=\\frac{359229046020947}{10^{15}},\\quad(D,r,j,q,s_0,E_D)=(17642,600782,51837,17555,5495,3559710).$$ Then $$\\sum_{z=0}^{202}\\binom{D-87z+2}{2}-r(D+1)=10599598107-10599596826=1281,$$ $$C_0=DM+(q+s_0-1)\\Lambda+(p-q-s_0+1)E_D=885213733790732.$$ Moreover, $$\\delta_7=\\frac{7949939667036172399086139222913311}{95621000000000000000000000000000000},$$ $$\\varepsilon_7-\\frac{C_0}{N}-\\delta_7=\\frac{67333805766276738068309588974841569}{153293031444312855941000000000000000000000000000000}>0.$$ For $\\tau_7=\\varepsilon_7/10$, $\\alpha=17643/147458$, $\\beta=5495/147457$, $c=\\alpha/\\beta$, $\\gamma^2=5495/(147457\\cdot17643)$, and $$F_7(a)=(\\beta-a)^2-\\gamma^2(1-a)(1-ca),$$ one has $$F_7(\\tau_7)=\\frac{310822941801540312341284744748980665822691}{5656809599924727240600000000000000000000000000000000}>0,$$ and $\\lceil M\\tau_7\\rceil=781092078$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-count-semantics","cc-r7-arithmetic-ledger"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P10"}],"id":"cc-r7-source-theorem","kind":"literature_input","label":"Doubly audited R7 source theorem","notes":"This is the exact indexed P10 statement, not a lower neighboring-cell strengthening.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P10.1"],"statement_markdown":"For every instance $c$, $$\\frac{A(c)}N\\ge\\varepsilon_7\\Longrightarrow\\frac{G(f)}M\\ge\\frac{\\varepsilon_7}{10}.$$ Hence $\\operatorname{Sound}(\\varepsilon_7)$ and $G(f)\\ge781092078$ under the displayed acceptance hypothesis.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-aligned-rounding","cc-r7-source-theorem"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-r7-source-cell","kind":"theorem","label":"Whole R7 source count cell","notes":"This is an elementary count-cell corollary, not a separately indexed source theorem.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $$k_7=1151782755825594,\\qquad r_7=781092077.$$ Then $k_7-1=r_7H+922933$ and $$\\left(\\frac{1151782755825593}{3206262880419842},\\frac{575891377912797}{1603131440209921}\\right]\\cap\\mathbb Q\\subseteq\\mathcal S.$$ In particular, $$\\varepsilon_7^*=\\frac{35922904602094685}{10^{17}}\\in\\mathcal S$$ because $$35922904602094685N-10^{17}(k_7-1)=2874745436739770>0,$$ $\\varepsilon_7^*<\\varepsilon_7$, and $\\lceil M\\varepsilon_7^*/10\\rceil=781092078$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-ambient"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P7"}],"id":"cc-incidence-mixing","kind":"lemma","label":"Exact affine incidence mixing","notes":"This universal form is reusable beyond the source-specific R7 core.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P7.1"],"statement_markdown":"For $Y\\subseteq X$ and $T\\subseteq\\mathcal L$, put $a=|Y|/M$, $b=|T|/\\Lambda$, and $J(Y,T)=I(Y,T)/N$. Then $$|J(Y,T)-ab|\\le\\sqrt{\\frac{a(1-a)b(1-b)}{p+1}}.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-r7-arithmetic-ledger"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-r7-tight-endpoints","kind":"lemma","label":"Tight hypergeometric endpoint bounds","notes":"Exact alternating-binomial replay establishes the displayed inequalities locally, but no stable hash-bound certificate stores them.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For $P_0=p+1$, $r=600782$, and $$H_a=\\frac{\\binom{\\Lambda-a}{r}}{\\binom{\\Lambda}{r}},$$ one has $$H_{51837}<\\frac{2387626371315326}{10^{16}},\\qquad H_{P_0}<\\frac{170031583622226}{10^{16}}.$$","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["cc-r7-tight-endpoints"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-r7-envelope-certificate","kind":"lemma","label":"Finite pencil-energy envelope","notes":"This is a finite family of $147459$ exact rational inequalities. R7 P2 states only its fixed-score consequence.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $\\phi_a=aH_a$ and $j=51837$. For every integer $0\\le a\\le P_0$, $$\\phi_a\\le\\frac{(P_0-a)\\phi_j+(a-j)\\phi_{P_0}}{P_0-j}.$$","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["cc-r7-envelope-certificate"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-r7-parametric-energy","kind":"lemma","label":"Acceptance-parametric energy selection","notes":"The fixed-score P2 hash is intentionally absent from this strengthened statement.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For every acceptance graph $E$ with $A=|E|/N\\ge j/P_0$, there is an $r$-line set $R$ such that, if $U_R$ counts accepted incidences at points whose accepted pencils miss $R$, then $$\\frac{U_R}{N}<\\Delta_*(A):=\\frac{j(1-A)h_j^*+(P_0A-j)h_P^*}{P_0-j},$$ where $$h_j^*=\\frac{2387626371315326}{10^{16}},\\qquad h_P^*=\\frac{170031583622226}{10^{16}}.$$","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["cc-r7-arithmetic-ledger","cc-r7-parametric-energy"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-r7-two-incidence-arithmetic","kind":"lemma","label":"Two-incidence exact rational boundary","notes":"The negative neighboring value shows that these endpoint bounds alone cannot gain a third incidence.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $$k_2=1151782755825592,\\qquad A_2=k_2/N,\\qquad r_7=781092077.$$ Then $k_2-1=r_7H+922931$, the affine function $A\\mapsto A-C_0/N-\\Delta_*(A)$ is strictly increasing, and $$A_2-\\frac{C_0}{N}-\\Delta_*(A_2)=\\frac{24329817599601268271}{383232578610782139852500000000000000}>0,$$ whereas $$\\frac{k_2-1}{N}-\\frac{C_0}{N}-\\Delta_*\\!\\left(\\frac{k_2-1}{N}\\right)=\\frac{-430133165077648103093}{1532930314443128559410000000000000000}<0.$$","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["cc-r7-arithmetic-ledger"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-r7-generic-core","kind":"obligation","label":"Score-independent R7 core ledger","notes":"R7 P3--P6 provide source-specific ancestry, but no indexed step states this universal implication.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For every acceptance graph $E$ and every $r$-line set $R$, if $$|E|>U_R+C_0,$$ then there is a nonempty subgraph with minimum point and line degrees $(17643,5495)$ carrying a primitive squarefree polynomial $B$ of weighted degree at most $17642$, formal line-label roots, and $B_Z(x,f(x))\\ne0$ at every retained point.","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["cc-incidence-mixing","cc-r7-arithmetic-ledger"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-r7-generic-mass","kind":"obligation","label":"Generic component-mass transfer","notes":"R7 P8 proves this only for the exact P6 core, so its hash is intentionally absent.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Every connected component of any nonempty affine-incidence subgraph with minimum point and line degrees $(17643,5495)$ has point density greater than $\\tau_7$ and therefore contains at least $781092078$ point vertices.","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["cc-r7-generic-core"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-r7-generic-recovery","kind":"obligation","label":"Generic simple-root recovery","notes":"R7 P9 is source-core-specific; the invariant-parametric KTZ lifting statement still needs its own indexed proof.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Every connected component of a core satisfying `cc-r7-generic-core` is labeled on all its point vertices by one polynomial $Q\\in F[X,Y]$ of total degree at most $87$.","work_state":"open"},{"dependencies":["cc-aligned-rounding","cc-r7-parametric-energy","cc-r7-two-incidence-arithmetic","cc-r7-generic-core","cc-r7-generic-mass","cc-r7-generic-recovery"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-r7-two-incidence-cell","kind":"theorem","label":"R7 two-incidence refinement","notes":"This is the strongest substantive round-6 target and remains blocked by the exact strengthened interfaces.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"blocked","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For every instance $c$, $$A(c)\\ge1151782755825592\\Longrightarrow G(f)\\ge781092078.$$ Consequently, $$\\left(\\frac{1151782755825591}{3206262880419842},\\frac{575891377912796}{1603131440209921}\\right]\\cap\\mathbb Q\\subseteq\\mathcal S.$$ In particular, $$\\widehat\\varepsilon_2=\\frac{3592290460209463}{10^{16}}\\in\\mathcal S$$ because $$3592290460209463N-10^{16}(k_2-1)=2653028701364846>0,$$ $$10^{16}k_2-3592290460209463N=7346971298635154>0,$$ and $\\lceil M\\widehat\\varepsilon_2/10\\rceil=781092078$.","work_state":"blocked"},{"dependencies":["cc-certificate-schema"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-r7-direct-artifact","kind":"obligation","label":"Hash-bound two-incidence UNSAT artifact","notes":"This is an analytic-independent alternative to the generic R7 bridge. No required formula or proof artifact is stored.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"blocked","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For $$k_2=1151782755825592,\\qquad r_7=781092077,$$ canonical generated bytes, checker bytes, a complete UNSAT proof $\\pi$, and a length-and-digest manifest satisfy all validations and $$\\operatorname{Check}_{\\mathrm{unsat}}(F_{k_2,r_7},\\pi)=\\mathrm{true}.$$","work_state":"blocked"},{"dependencies":["cc-count-semantics"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0004","source_response_sha256":"d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","source_step_id":"P15"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0005","source_response_sha256":"f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","source_step_id":"P19"}],"id":"cc-histogram-certificate","kind":"lemma","label":"Constant-polynomial integer certificate","notes":"This is a $p$-variable pigeonhole certificate independent of acceptance.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0004:P15.1","researcher-0005:P19.1"],"statement_markdown":"For $n_b(f)=|\\{x:f(x)=b\\}|$, the integer system $$\\sum_{b\\in F}n_b=M,\\qquad0\\le n_b\\le p-1$$ is infeasible. Hence some constant polynomial agrees with $f$ on at least $p$ points, so $$G(f)\\ge p,\\qquad\\operatorname{Agr}_{87}(f)\\ge\\frac1p.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-histogram-certificate"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-trivial-score-family","kind":"theorem","label":"Universal low-score interval","notes":"The acceptance hypothesis is unused.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Every rational $\\varepsilon$ satisfying $$0<\\varepsilon\\le\\frac{10}{147457}$$ belongs to $\\mathcal S$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-trivial-score-family"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-no-least-score","kind":"theorem","label":"No lowest positive score","notes":"The sound terminating decimals $10^{-n}$ for $n\\ge5$ already converge to zero.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"The rational sound-score set satisfies $$\\inf\\mathcal S=0$$ and has no least element. The same conclusion holds after restricting admissible scores to positive terminating decimals.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-aligned-rounding"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0004","source_response_sha256":"d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","source_step_id":"P12"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0005","source_response_sha256":"f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","source_step_id":"P18"}],"id":"cc-adversarial-gap","kind":"theorem","label":"Exact nonsound interval","notes":"This accepted construction demonstrates that the literal score predicate is nonmonotone.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0004:P12.1","researcher-0005:P18.1"],"statement_markdown":"There exists an instance $c$ such that $$A(c)\\ge88\\Lambda=1913446858928,\n\\qquad G(f)\\le2p-1=294913.$$ Consequently, $$\\left[\\frac{20}{147457},\\frac{88}{147457}\\right]\\cap\\mathbb Q$$ is disjoint from $\\mathcal S$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["cc-profile-reduction","cc-ip-equivalence","cc-exhaustive-profile","cc-r7-source-cell","cc-no-least-score","cc-adversarial-gap"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"cc-exact-score-set","kind":"theorem","label":"Exact finite characterization and literal target resolution","notes":"Raw enumeration is infeasible in practice. The certificate branch gives an independently checkable route for selected cells; the two-incidence cell remains open.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"The rational sound-score set is exactly $$\\mathcal S=\\mathbb Q\\cap\\bigcup_{\\substack{1\\le k\\le N\\\\C_{\\lfloor(k-1)/H\\rfloor}<k}}\\left(\\frac{k-1}{N},\\frac{k}{N}\\right]$$ $$=\\mathbb Q\\cap\\bigcup_{\\substack{1\\le k\\le N\\\\\\operatorname{BadIP}(k,\\lfloor(k-1)/H\\rfloor)\\ \\mathrm{infeasible}}}\\left(\\frac{k-1}{N},\\frac{k}{N}\\right].$$ Every indexing predicate is decidable by exact finite enumeration. Moreover, $(0,10/147457]\\cap\\mathbb Q\\subseteq\\mathcal S$, the complete R7 source cell lies in $\\mathcal S$, and $[20/147457,88/147457]\\cap\\mathbb Q$ is nonsound. Therefore the requested lowest positive rational or terminating-decimal soundness score does not exist.","work_state":"candidate"}],"progress":{"blocked":0,"invalid":0,"mapped":4,"open":12,"percent":20,"provisional":0,"total":15,"verified":3},"render_validation":{"math_segments":212,"messages":4,"passed":true,"roadmaps":1},"roadmap_id":"certified-computation","round":6,"summary":"$4f","target_statement":"At $m=2$, $p=147457$, and total degree $87$, characterize the rational sound-score set by exact finite profiles and bad-instance integer programs; provide sound hash-bound SAT, UNSAT, and rational-arithmetic certificate interfaces; record the accepted R7 source cell and the blocked two-incidence refinement; and prove that the literal lowest-positive-$\\varepsilon$ objective has no solution.","title":"Certified finite computation","updated_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z"},{"corpus_sha256":"ea74c83b4a458f21070007b5661f3dc825852d26afbb96773d309aa1f3e16ed5","critical_path":["e2e-00-prime-certificate","e2e-01-protocol","e2e-04-fixed-arithmetic","e2e-04-energy-envelope","e2e-05-energy-selection","e2e-03-rigidity-input","e2e-06-squarefree-interpolant","e2e-07-identity-transfer","e2e-08-primitive-cleanup","e2e-09-earliest-deletion","e2e-10-amortized-survival","e2e-10-simple-root-core","e2e-02-incidence-mixing","e2e-12-component-mass","e2e-11-lifting-input","e2e-13-one-global-polynomial","e2e-14-source-soundness","e2e-14-numeric-agreement","e2e-15-goal"],"focus":"a complete fixed-parameter dependency chain ending in one global polynomial","goal_node_id":"e2e-15-goal","messages":[{"body_markdown":"The round-6 snapshot has $138$ stable steps and $68$ double accepts, exactly from researchers 0004--0008. R7 P10 remains the lowest accepted acceptance-driven source theorem. R9 P13 has no audits, while R10 is `revise, revise` and numerically weaker than R7; neither changes the accepted frontier.","channel":"global","in_reply_to":"msg-8e6d486e9f3b","kind":"reply","references":["research_state/campaign-10-ultra/roadmaps/corpus-index.json","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","researcher-0009|P13|da89baf01629f789c4e9b56d186509a33896212a6b7f0f105aedf3431f4d8b03","researcher-0010|P10|a011600739e25d4ffa0074a86b31b5861524f97eb2ef11ef1a68fd711533c8a2"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-14-source-soundness","e2e-15-goal","e2e-28-pencil-gap-extension"],"subject":"Round-6 evidence boundary"},{"body_markdown":"Joint acceptance and recovery integrality extends R7 P10 to the whole cell, not merely to $\\varepsilon\\le\\varepsilon_7$. With $C=1474580$, $$k_7-1=781092077C+922933,$$ so the source conclusion forces $781092078$ agreement points, enough throughout $$\\frac{k_7-1}{N}<\\varepsilon\\le\\frac{k_7}{N}.$$ The terminating value $0.35922904602094685$ lies in this cell. This deduction remains separate from the P10 evidence triple.","channel":"certified-computation","in_reply_to":"msg-bbe7290b676a","kind":"reply","references":["certified-computation/cc-r7-source-cell","researcher-0007|P10|b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-14-source-soundness","e2e-14-numeric-agreement","e2e-15-goal"],"subject":"Use the full joint count cell"},{"body_markdown":"The proposed $k_2=1151782755825592$ refinement still requires hypothesis-parametric energy, a score-independent core ledger, generic component mass, and generic recovery. Nodes `e2e-22-parametric-energy` through `e2e-27-two-incidence-frontier` therefore retain empty evidence references: accepted R7 P2, P6, P8, and P9 state only the fixed source regime.","channel":"exact-analytic","in_reply_to":"msg-d695a051ce00","kind":"request","references":["exact-analytic/ea-62-r7-tight-endpoints","exact-analytic/ea-63-r7-tight-parametric-energy","exact-analytic/ea-54-r7-generic-ledger","exact-analytic/ea-56-r7-generic-mass","exact-analytic/ea-57-r7-generic-recovery"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-22-parametric-energy","e2e-23-generic-ledger","e2e-24-generic-component-mass","e2e-25-generic-recovery","e2e-27-two-incidence-frontier"],"subject":"Audit the two-incidence interfaces"},{"body_markdown":"Please audit researcher-0009 P13 independently. It claims a table with $$\\operatorname{Pass}\\ge\\frac{13123585}{21743566849},\\qquad \\operatorname{Agr}_{87}<\\frac6{147457},$$ extending the known nonsound interval to $[20/147457,13123585/21743566849]$ when combined with R4 P12. The claim currently has no verifier verdict.","channel":"exact-analytic","in_reply_to":null,"kind":"request","references":["researcher-0009|P13|da89baf01629f789c4e9b56d186509a33896212a6b7f0f105aedf3431f4d8b03","researcher-0004|P12|d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626"],"related_node_ids":["e2e-18-adversarial-gap","e2e-28-pencil-gap-extension"],"subject":"Audit the R9 pencil obstruction"}],"nodes":[{"dependencies":[],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P1"}],"id":"e2e-00-prime-certificate","kind":"lemma","label":"Fixed prime certificate","notes":"Pocklington supplies the fixed field used throughout the chain.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P1.1"],"statement_markdown":"Let $p=147457$. The identities $$p-1=2^{14}3^2,$$ $$10^{p-1}\\equiv1\\pmod p,\\quad 10^{(p-1)/2}\\equiv147456\\pmod p,\\quad 10^{(p-1)/3}\\equiv78348\\pmod p,$$ and $$\\gcd(147455,p)=\\gcd(78347,p)=1$$ imply that $p$ is prime.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-00-prime-certificate"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P1"}],"id":"e2e-01-protocol","kind":"definition","label":"Fixed protocol and soundness predicate","notes":"All probabilities use the uniform affine-line-then-uniform-point incidence distribution.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P1.1"],"statement_markdown":"Set $F=\\mathbb F_{147457}$, $$M:=p^2=21743566849,\\quad P_0:=p+1=147458,$$ $$\\Lambda:=pP_0=21743714306,\\quad N:=p\\Lambda=3206262880419842.$$ For $f:F^2\\to F$ and degree-at-most-$87$ line labels $P_L$, let $$E:=\\{(x,L):x\\in L,\\ P_L(x)=f(x)\\},\\qquad \\operatorname{Pass}(f,P):=\\frac{|E|}{N},$$ and $$\\operatorname{Agr}_{87}(f):=\\max_{\\deg_{\\mathrm{total}}Q\\le87}\\Pr_{x\\in F^2}[Q(x)=f(x)].$$ Put $$\\varepsilon_7:=\\frac{359229046020947}{10^{15}},\\qquad \\tau_7:=\\frac{\\varepsilon_7}{10}.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-01-protocol"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P1"}],"id":"e2e-04-fixed-arithmetic","kind":"lemma","label":"R7 fixed arithmetic ledger","notes":"These are the single fixed choices used in the accepted R7 chain.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P1.1"],"statement_markdown":"Set $$D:=17642,\\quad r:=600782,\\quad j:=51837,\\quad s:=5495,$$ $$q:=D-87=17555,\\qquad z_{\\max}:=\\left\\lfloor\\frac D{87}\\right\\rfloor=202.$$ Then $$V_D:=\\sum_{z=0}^{202}\\binom{D-87z+2}{2}=10599598107,$$ $$r(D+1)=10599596826,\\quad V_D-r(D+1)=1281,\\quad r>D,$$ and $$E_D:=(202-1)(2D-87\\cdot202)=3559710.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-04-fixed-arithmetic"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P2"}],"id":"e2e-04-energy-envelope","kind":"lemma","label":"Whole-pencil hypergeometric envelope","notes":"The global chord controls every possible accepted degree of a point.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P2.1"],"statement_markdown":"For $0\\le a\\le P_0$, define $$H_a:=\\frac{\\binom{\\Lambda-a}{r}}{\\binom{\\Lambda}{r}},\\qquad \\phi_a:=aH_a.$$ Put $$h_j:=\\frac{238762637131533}{10^{15}},\\qquad h_{P_0}:=\\frac{17003158362223}{10^{15}}.$$ Then $H_j<h_j$, $H_{P_0}<h_{P_0}$, and $$\\phi_a\\le\\frac{(P_0-a)jH_j+(a-j)P_0H_{P_0}}{P_0-j}$$ for every integer $a\\in[0,P_0]$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-04-energy-envelope"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P2"}],"id":"e2e-05-energy-selection","kind":"reduction","label":"Exact-size line selection","notes":"Missed accepted pencils are the only loss charged at this stage.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P2.1"],"statement_markdown":"For $N_E(x):=\\{L:(x,L)\\in E\\}$ and an $r$-line set $R$, put $$U_R:=\\sum_{x:N_E(x)\\cap R=\\varnothing}|N_E(x)|.$$ If $\\operatorname{Pass}(f,P)\\ge\\varepsilon_7$, there exists $R\\subseteq\\mathcal L$ with $|R|=600782$ and $$\\frac{U_R}{N}<\\delta_7,$$ where $$\\delta_7:=\\frac{7949939667036172399086139222913311}{95621000000000000000000000000000000}.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-05-energy-selection"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P3"}],"id":"e2e-03-rigidity-input","kind":"literature_input","label":"Source-specific line rigidity","notes":"This is the precise rigidity interface imported by R7 P3.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P3.1"],"statement_markdown":"If $S\\in F[X,Y]$ has total degree at most $D$ and vanishes formally on more than $D$ distinct affine lines, then $S=0$. Since $|R|=r>D$, every nonzero weighted interpolation relation vanishing on all selected labeled-line graphs depends on $Z$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-03-rigidity-input"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P3"}],"id":"e2e-06-squarefree-interpolant","kind":"lemma","label":"Squarefree weighted relation","notes":"Minimum weighted degree is taken over every eligible relation with nonzero $Z$-derivative.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P3.1"],"statement_markdown":"There exists a nonzero squarefree polynomial $\\mathcal A\\in F[X,Y,Z]$ such that $$\\operatorname{wdeg}_{(1,1,87)}\\mathcal A\\le D,\\qquad \\mathcal A_Z\\ne0,$$ and $$\\mathcal A(L(t),P_L(t))\\equiv0\\qquad(L\\in R).$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-06-squarefree-interpolant"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P4"}],"id":"e2e-07-identity-transfer","kind":"reduction","label":"Mass-preserving identity transfer","notes":"Every excluded line is charged by at most $D$ hit incidences.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P4.1"],"statement_markdown":"Call $(x,L)\\in E$ hit when $N_E(x)\\cap R\\ne\\varnothing$. Let $T$ contain $R$ and every $L\\notin R$ with more than $D$ hit accepted incidences; put $t:=|T|$ and $E_T:=\\{(x,L)\\in E:L\\in T\\}$. Then $$\\mathcal A(L(t),P_L(t))\\equiv0\\qquad(L\\in T)$$ and $$|E|\\le |E_T|+U_R+D(\\Lambda-t).$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-07-identity-transfer"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P5"}],"id":"e2e-08-primitive-cleanup","kind":"lemma","label":"Primitive discriminant cleanup","notes":"The nominal-degree discriminant handles leading-coefficient drops without division.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P5.1"],"statement_markdown":"Write $\\mathcal A=CB$, where $C\\in F[X,Y]$ is the coefficient content in $Z$ and $B$ is primitive. Then $B$ is squarefree, $$\\operatorname{wdeg}_{(1,1,87)}B\\le D,\\quad \\deg_ZB\\le202<p,\\quad \\gcd(B,B_Z)=1.$$ There is $\\mathcal E\\subseteq T$, with $e:=|\\mathcal E|\\le E_D$, such that every $L\\in T\\setminus\\mathcal E$ satisfies $$B(L(t),P_L(t))\\equiv0,$$ while $B_Z(L(t),P_L(t))$ is nonzero of degree at most $q=17555$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-08-primitive-cleanup"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P6"}],"id":"e2e-09-earliest-deletion","kind":"lemma","label":"Earliest-deletion charge","notes":"Each removed edge is charged at its first applicable deletion rule.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P6.1"],"statement_markdown":"Delete all edges on $\\mathcal E$, all remaining $(x,L)\\in E_T$ with $B_Z(x,f(x))=0$, and then iteratively points of current degree at most $D$ and lines of current degree at most $s-1$. If every edge is deleted, then $$|E_T|\\le pe+q(t-e)+DM+(s-1)(t-e).$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-09-earliest-deletion"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P6"}],"id":"e2e-10-amortized-survival","kind":"reduction","label":"Exact R7 survival ledger","notes":"The strict rational surplus rules out complete deletion.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P6.1"],"statement_markdown":"Complete deletion implies $$|E|\\le U_R+C_0,$$ where $$C_0:=DM+(q+s-1)\\Lambda+(p-q-s+1)E_D=885213733790732.$$ Moreover, $$\\varepsilon_7-\\frac{C_0}{N}-\\delta_7=\\frac{67333805766276738068309588974841569}{153293031444312855941000000000000000000000000000000}>0.$$ Hence $\\operatorname{Pass}(f,P)\\ge\\varepsilon_7$ makes complete deletion impossible.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-10-amortized-survival"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P6"}],"id":"e2e-10-simple-root-core","kind":"reduction","label":"Nonempty simple-root core","notes":"This records exactly the structural output needed by mixing and recovery.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P6.1"],"statement_markdown":"There is a nonempty retained graph $$G_*=(X_*,\\mathcal T_*,E_*)$$ of minimum point degree at least $D+1=17643$ and minimum line degree at least $s=5495$ such that $$B(L(t),P_L(t))\\equiv0\\qquad(L\\in\\mathcal T_*),$$ and every $x\\in X_*$ satisfies $$B(x,f(x))=0,\\qquad B_Z(x,f(x))\\ne0.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-10-simple-root-core"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P7"}],"id":"e2e-02-incidence-mixing","kind":"lemma","label":"Centered affine incidence mixing","notes":"The universal mixing inequality is placed at its first use in the spine.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P7.1"],"statement_markdown":"For $X\\subseteq F^2$ and a line set $S$, let $a:=|X|/M$ and $b:=|S|/\\Lambda$. Their ambient incidence count satisfies $$\\frac{I(X,S)}N\\le ab+\\sqrt{\\frac{a(1-a)b(1-b)}{P_0}}.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-02-incidence-mixing"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P8"}],"id":"e2e-12-component-mass","kind":"lemma","label":"Every source core component is large","notes":"The integer form is the agreement count later used for joint cell rounding.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P8.1"],"statement_markdown":"Every connected component $K=(X_K,\\mathcal T_K,E_K)$ of $G_*$ satisfies $$\\frac{|X_K|}{M}>\\tau_7.$$ Consequently, every component contains at least $781092078$ point vertices.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-12-component-mass"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P9"}],"id":"e2e-11-lifting-input","kind":"literature_input","label":"Source-specific simple-root reconstruction","notes":"This is applied only to the exact P6 core; generic reuse is separated below.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"external","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P9.1"],"statement_markdown":"Let $K$ be a connected component of $G_*$ and $b\\in X_K$. The at least $D+1$ incident degree-at-most-$87$ line labels are formal roots of $B$ with common simple value $f(b)$. There exists $Q_K\\in F[X,Y]$ of total degree at most $87$ satisfying $$B(X,Y,Q_K(X,Y))\\equiv0$$ and agreeing with every seed-line label. At every reached point, simple-root uniqueness identifies $Q_K$ with each adjacent line label.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-11-lifting-input"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P9"}],"id":"e2e-13-one-global-polynomial","kind":"lemma","label":"One global polynomial on a component","notes":"Selecting one component is sufficient; different components need not share their polynomial.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P9.1"],"statement_markdown":"For every connected component $K$ of $G_*$, there exists one polynomial $$Q_K\\in F[X,Y],\\qquad \\deg_{\\mathrm{total}}Q_K\\le87,$$ such that $$Q_K(x)=f(x)\\qquad(x\\in X_K).$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-13-one-global-polynomial"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P10"}],"id":"e2e-14-source-soundness","kind":"theorem","label":"R7 source soundness theorem","notes":"This node matches the indexed P10 endpoint statement.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P10.1"],"statement_markdown":"For every fixed-instance point and line table, $$\\operatorname{Pass}(f,P)\\ge\\varepsilon_7\\Longrightarrow\\exists Q\\in F[X,Y],\\ \\deg_{\\mathrm{total}}Q\\le87:\\ \\Pr_x[Q(x)=f(x)]\\ge\\frac{\\varepsilon_7}{10}.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-14-source-soundness"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"e2e-14-numeric-agreement","kind":"lemma","label":"Joint acceptance and recovery cell alignment","notes":"This is an elementary integer deduction from P10, not an indexed source step.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $$C:=10P_0=1474580,\\quad k_7:=1151782755825594,\\quad r_7:=781092077.$$ The identities $$359229046020947N=(k_7-1)10^{15}+509686886430374,$$ $$359229046020947M=r_7\\,10^{16}+6258958548786003,$$ and $$k_7-1=r_7C+922933$$ give $$\\lceil N\\varepsilon_7\\rceil=k_7,\\qquad \\left\\lceil\\frac{M\\varepsilon_7}{10}\\right\\rceil=r_7+1.$$ Thus, for every rational $$(k_7-1)/N<\\varepsilon\\le k_7/N,$$ the hypothesis $\\operatorname{Pass}(f,P)\\ge\\varepsilon$ forces $|E|\\ge k_7$ and hence the source theorem, while $$\\frac{M\\varepsilon}{10}\\le\\frac{k_7}{C}<r_7+1.$$ Therefore its polynomial has agreement at least $\\varepsilon/10$. Finally, for $$\\varepsilon_*:=\\frac{35922904602094685}{10^{17}},$$ $$35922904602094685N-(k_7-1)10^{17}=2874745436739770>0,$$ $$k_7 10^{17}-35922904602094685N=97125254563260230>0,$$ so $\\varepsilon_*$ lies in this cell.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-14-numeric-agreement"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"e2e-15-goal","kind":"theorem","label":"Full R7 count-cell soundness","notes":"The open lower endpoint means this substantive cell has an infimum but no least rational representative.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For every rational $$\\frac{1151782755825593}{3206262880419842}<\\varepsilon\\le\\frac{1151782755825594}{3206262880419842}=\\frac{575891377912797}{1603131440209921},$$ every $f:F^2\\to F$ and every degree-at-most-$87$ affine-line table satisfy $$\\operatorname{Pass}(f,P)\\ge\\varepsilon\\Longrightarrow\\exists Q\\in F[X,Y],\\ \\deg_{\\mathrm{total}}Q\\le87:\\ \\Pr_{x\\in F^2}[Q(x)=f(x)]\\ge\\frac{\\varepsilon}{10}.$$ In particular, the implication holds at $$\\varepsilon_*=0.35922904602094685.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-01-protocol"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0005","source_response_sha256":"f61c23bd178746fa6c6757cb8e74d13d76d67cc3fe8075b8dcc8e4da0c470095","source_step_id":"P19"}],"id":"e2e-16-constant-floor","kind":"lemma","label":"Universal constant-polynomial floor","notes":"This conclusion is independent of the line table and its acceptance probability.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0005:P19.1"],"statement_markdown":"Every $f:F^2\\to F$ agrees with some constant polynomial on at least a $1/147457$ fraction of $F^2$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-16-constant-floor"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"e2e-17-no-lowest-score","kind":"theorem","label":"The literal score set has no minimum","notes":"This resolves the specification-level optimization separately from the substantive R7 cell.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $\\mathcal S\\subseteq\\mathbb Q\\cap(0,1]$ be the scores satisfying the target implication. Then $$(0,10/147457]\\cap\\mathbb Q\\subseteq\\mathcal S.$$ Hence $\\inf\\mathcal S=0$, and neither the positive rational scores nor the positive terminating-decimal scores have a least element.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-01-protocol"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0004","source_response_sha256":"d6bc64ab60bac8fd0da8237c80f8bde4a4d6f18f1c9d8b23b9cb4b718006f626","source_step_id":"P12"}],"id":"e2e-18-adversarial-gap","kind":"theorem","label":"Accepted nonmonotonicity obstruction","notes":"The constant-floor interval is not the beginning of a monotone soundness range.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0004:P12.1"],"statement_markdown":"There exist $f$ and a degree-at-most-$87$ line table satisfying $$\\operatorname{Pass}(f,P)\\ge\\frac{88}{147457},\\qquad \\operatorname{Agr}_{87}(f)<\\frac2{147457}.$$ Consequently, the target implication fails for every $$\\varepsilon\\in\\left[\\frac{20}{147457},\\frac{88}{147457}\\right].$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-01-protocol"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0006","source_response_sha256":"5be5e5dcf77e673f21aa1a7eb4b15ff73cbdd9a702eef31a90d1bc2367af356c","source_step_id":"P10"}],"id":"e2e-19-verified-baseline","kind":"theorem","label":"Independent R6 fallback","notes":"This preserves a separate accepted architecture, although R7 is numerically stronger.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0006:P10.1"],"statement_markdown":"If $$\\operatorname{Pass}(f,P)\\ge\\frac{5759100500000001}{10^{16}},$$ then some $Q\\in F[X,Y]$ of total degree at most $87$ satisfies $$\\Pr_x[Q(x)=f(x)]\\ge\\frac{5759100500000001}{10^{17}}.$$","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-04-energy-envelope"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P11"},{"source_job_id":"researcher-0007","source_response_sha256":"b0307079501fb1093eed46812c7806a002c9dde4c0167606fd51dca9249927e0","source_step_id":"P12"}],"id":"e2e-20-point-degree-barrier","kind":"lemma","label":"Point-degree relaxation barrier","notes":"This does not rule out improvements using line-side, adaptive, or polynomial-label structure.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"verified","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0007:P11.1","researcher-0007:P12.1"],"statement_markdown":"The affine point-line incidence graph of $F^2$ contains no $K_{2,2}$. Moreover, for every family of integers $(a_x)_{x\\in F^2}$ with $0\\le a_x\\le P_0$, there is an incidence subgraph whose point degrees are exactly $(a_x)_{x\\in F^2}$.","work_state":"candidate"},{"dependencies":["e2e-04-energy-envelope"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"e2e-21-tight-endpoints","kind":"obligation","label":"Tight hypergeometric endpoints","notes":"These sharper rational bounds are not the endpoint bounds stated by the indexed R7 P2.","owner":"certified-computation","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Prove $$H_j<\\frac{2387626371315326}{10^{16}},\\qquad H_{P_0}<\\frac{170031583622226}{10^{16}}.$$","work_state":"drafting"},{"dependencies":["e2e-21-tight-endpoints"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"e2e-22-parametric-energy","kind":"obligation","label":"Acceptance-parametric energy selection","notes":"A fixed-score P2 evidence reference would not match this strengthened statement.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Put $$h_j^*:=\\frac{2387626371315326}{10^{16}},\\qquad h_P^*:=\\frac{170031583622226}{10^{16}},$$ and $$\\Delta^*(A):=\\frac{j(1-A)h_j^*+(P_0A-j)h_P^*}{P_0-j}.$$ For every $j/P_0\\le A\\le1$, prove that $\\operatorname{Pass}(f,P)\\ge A$ yields an $r$-line set $R$ satisfying $$\\frac{U_R}{N}<\\Delta^*(A).$$","work_state":"open"},{"dependencies":["e2e-09-earliest-deletion"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"e2e-23-generic-ledger","kind":"obligation","label":"Score-independent interpolation and peeling ledger","notes":"This packages the P3--P6 construction for an arbitrary $r$-line set returned by a parametric selector.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For every $r$-line set $R$, construct the weighted relation and primitive cleanup so that either a nonempty core with the properties of `e2e-10-simple-root-core` survives, or $$|E|\\le U_R+C_0.$$","work_state":"open"},{"dependencies":["e2e-02-incidence-mixing"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"e2e-24-generic-component-mass","kind":"obligation","label":"Generic component-mass transfer","notes":"R7 P8 is stated for its source P6 core, so its hash is not attached to this schema.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Prove that every connected component of any nonempty core having minimum degrees $(17643,5495)$ contains at least $781092078$ point vertices.","work_state":"open"},{"dependencies":["e2e-11-lifting-input"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"e2e-25-generic-recovery","kind":"obligation","label":"Generic one-polynomial recovery","notes":"R7 P9 is source-core-specific; this is the required invariant-transfer form.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"open","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For any connected core carrying the displayed formal $B$-identities and pointwise simple roots, prove that one $Q\\in F[X,Y]$ of total degree at most $87$ satisfies $Q(x)=f(x)$ at every point vertex of that component.","work_state":"open"},{"dependencies":["e2e-22-parametric-energy","e2e-23-generic-ledger","e2e-24-generic-component-mass","e2e-25-generic-recovery"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"e2e-21-one-edge-obligation","kind":"obligation","label":"One-edge lower trigger","notes":"This preserves the previous one-edge target; the two-incidence target below would subsume it.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"blocked","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $k_+:=1151782755825593$. Prove that $|E|\\ge k_+$ yields a polynomial $Q\\in F[X,Y]$ of total degree at most $87$ agreeing with $f$ on at least $781092078$ points.","work_state":"blocked"},{"dependencies":["e2e-22-parametric-energy","e2e-23-generic-ledger"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"e2e-26-two-incidence-core","kind":"obligation","label":"Two-incidence lower core","notes":"The negative neighboring value is a limitation of this scalar relaxation, not a counterexample.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"blocked","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"Let $$k_2:=1151782755825592,\\qquad A_2:=\\frac{k_2}{N}.$$ Prove $$A_2-\\frac{C_0}{N}-\\Delta^*(A_2)=\\frac{24329817599601268271}{383232578610782139852500000000000000}>0.$$ Hence $|E|\\ge k_2$ forces a nonempty simple-root core. Also record that at $A_-:=(k_2-1)/N$, $$A_--\\frac{C_0}{N}-\\Delta^*(A_-)=\\frac{-430133165077648103093}{1532930314443128559410000000000000000}<0.$$","work_state":"blocked"},{"dependencies":["e2e-26-two-incidence-core","e2e-24-generic-component-mass","e2e-25-generic-recovery"],"evidence_refs":[],"id":"e2e-27-two-incidence-frontier","kind":"theorem","label":"Provisional two-incidence soundness frontier","notes":"This is the best current arithmetic candidate but remains blocked on four strengthened analytic interfaces.","owner":"end-to-end-soundness","proof_state":"blocked","resolved_lemma_ids":[],"statement_markdown":"For every rational $$(k_2-1)/N<\\varepsilon\\le\\varepsilon_7,$$ prove $$\\operatorname{Pass}(f,P)\\ge\\varepsilon\\Longrightarrow\\exists Q,\\ \\deg_{\\mathrm{total}}Q\\le87:\\ \\Pr_x[Q(x)=f(x)]\\ge\\frac{\\varepsilon}{10}.$$ In particular, for $$\\widehat\\varepsilon_2:=\\frac{3592290460209463}{10^{16}},$$ $$3592290460209463N-(k_2-1)10^{16}=2653028701364846>0,$$ $$k_2 10^{16}-3592290460209463N=7346971298635154>0,$$ and $$\\left\\lceil\\frac{M\\widehat\\varepsilon_2}{10}\\right\\rceil=781092078.$$","work_state":"blocked"},{"dependencies":["e2e-18-adversarial-gap"],"evidence_refs":[{"source_job_id":"researcher-0009","source_response_sha256":"da89baf01629f789c4e9b56d186509a33896212a6b7f0f105aedf3431f4d8b03","source_step_id":"P13"}],"id":"e2e-28-pencil-gap-extension","kind":"obligation","label":"Unaudited R9 nonsoundness extension","notes":"The stable source claim has no verifier audits in this corpus snapshot.","owner":"exact-analytic","proof_state":"provisional","resolved_lemma_ids":["researcher-0009:P13.1"],"statement_markdown":"Establish a table satisfying $$\\operatorname{Pass}(f,P)\\ge\\frac{13123585}{21743566849}=\\frac{89p-88}{p^2},\\qquad \\operatorname{Agr}_{87}(f)<\\frac6p.$$ It refutes the target for $[60/p,(89p-88)/p^2]$ and, together with `e2e-18-adversarial-gap`, for the entire interval $$\\left[\\frac{20}{p},\\frac{89p-88}{p^2}\\right].$$","work_state":"drafting"}],"progress":{"blocked":0,"invalid":0,"mapped":14,"open":2,"percent":87,"provisional":0,"total":16,"verified":14},"render_validation":{"math_segments":197,"messages":4,"passed":true,"roadmaps":1},"roadmap_id":"end-to-end-soundness","round":6,"summary":"$50","target_statement":"Prove that acceptance at least an explicit $\\varepsilon$ yields agreement with one total-degree-at-most-$87$ polynomial on at least $\\varepsilon/10$ of $\\mathbb F_{147457}^2$.","title":"End-to-end soundness chain","updated_at":"2026-09-15T02:36:18Z"}],"round":6,"schema":"line-point-proof-roadmaps-v1","status":"watching","updated_at":"2026-09-15T03:26:38Z"},"schema":"line-point-concrete-dashboard-v1","soundness_history":{"fixed_degree":87,"fixed_prime":147457,"lower_is_better":true,"points":[{"agreement_count":15567047720,"gain":0.28406191000000003,"job_id":"researcher-0004","previous_best":1,"recovery_agreement_count":1556704772,"soundness":0.71593809,"theorem_sha256":"34c7faff4866a1e320dba8f54350694e4a4d5b3f2237128daf83746dbca6a881","title":"Exact weighted interpolation and direct B_Z cleanup give soundness 0.71593809","verified_at":"2026-09-15T00:04:00Z","verifier_ids":["verifier-a-researcher-0004","verifier-b-researcher-0004"]},{"agreement_count":15437392452,"gain":0.005962925453699919,"job_id":"researcher-0005","previous_best":0.71593809,"recovery_agreement_count":1543739246,"soundness":0.7099751645463,"theorem_sha256":"0e2b06986a1dc8832d4a1806482f87692f9c355b57c76c1ef630426728db947c","title":"Discriminant and separability optimization of the fixed affine line-versus-point KTZ chain","verified_at":"2026-09-15T00:10:59Z","verifier_ids":["verifier-a-researcher-0005","verifier-b-researcher-0005"]},{"agreement_count":12522338672,"gain":0.1340651145463,"job_id":"researcher-0006","previous_best":0.70997516